window.REV_FLIP=window.REV_FLIP||{};window.REV_FLIP["fine-tuning-llm"]=[{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0001","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-001-overview","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s001","q":"What is the running example model in the Fine-Tuning for LLMs course, and which libraries does it use?","a":"<p><strong>FLAN-T5</strong>, used with Hugging Face and TensorFlow/Keras.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0002","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-001-overview","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s001","q":"What is the progression of techniques in the Fine-Tuning for LLMs course?","a":"<p>Prompting first, then transfer learning, then LoRA.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0003","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-001-overview","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s001","q":"When the lesson notes and the notebooks disagree in the FineTuningLLM course, which one is treated as ground truth?","a":"<p>The <strong>notebooks</strong> are ground truth, and the differences are flagged.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0004","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-002-1-course-map-core-stack","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s002","q":"What does each chapter of the Fine-Tuning for LLMs course cover?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Chapter</th><th>Topic</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>2</td><td>Prompting, few-shot / in-context learning with FLAN-T5</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>3</td><td>Transfer learning (freeze pre-trained layers)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>4</td><td>LoRA fine-tuning</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>5</td><td>Applications</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0005","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-002-1-course-map-core-stack","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s002","q":"What are the hands-on items for chapter 3 (transfer learning) of the Fine-Tuning for LLMs course?","a":"<p>Demo 1 (en→es, opus-100), Demo 2 (+ROUGE/BLEU), and the challenge WMT16 en→de.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0006","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-002-1-course-map-core-stack","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s002","q":"What are the hands-on items for chapter 4 (LoRA) of the Fine-Tuning for LLMs course?","a":"<p>Demo 1 (LoRA layer), Demo 2 (rank × batch-size experiments), and the challenge with a small model.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0007","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-002-1-course-map-core-stack","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s002","q":"What are the hands-on items for chapter 5 (applications) of the Fine-Tuning for LLMs course?","a":"<p>A chatbot (Flask), and the challenges DistilBERT SST-2, FLAN-T5 SQuAD v2 and LoRA summarisation.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0008","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-002-1-course-map-core-stack","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s002","q":"What are the hands-on items for chapter 2 of the Fine-Tuning for LLMs course?","a":"<p>Demo 1 (zero-shot), Demo 2 (few-shot), and the challenge few-shot translation.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0009","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-002-1-course-map-core-stack","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s002","q":"What is the core technology stack of the FLAN-T5 fine-tuning course?","a":"<p>FLAN-T5 (Google's instruction-tuned T5), Hugging Face <code>transformers</code>/<code>datasets</code>, TensorFlow/Keras, LoRA/PEFT, Flask, and Google Colab (free GPU, allocation varies).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0010","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-002-1-course-map-core-stack","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s002","q":"What is the end-to-end pipeline for adapting a pre-trained model in the FLAN-T5 course?","a":"<p>Pre-trained model → load dataset → tokenize → freeze layers (or add LoRA) → train with validation → evaluate (ROUGE/BLEU) → deploy.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0011","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-002-1-course-map-core-stack","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s002","q":"Which version gotchas affect the FLAN-T5 notebooks with <code>datasets</code>, the tokenizer and the optimizer?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><code>datasets.load_metric</code> is removed in newer <code>datasets</code>. Use <code>evaluate</code>.</li>\n  <li><code>tokenizer.as_target_tokenizer()</code> is deprecated. Use <code>text_target=</code>.</li>\n  <li>The notebooks import <code>tf_keras</code> for the optimizer because of the Keras 3 split.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0012","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-003-2-1-ethical-considerations","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s003","q":"What are the three ethical considerations for LLMs?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Bias in training data:</strong> LLMs reproduce biases in their data. Mitigate with curation and bias detection.</li>\n  <li><strong>Transparency:</strong> be able to explain how the model decides.</li>\n  <li><strong>Regulation:</strong> guidelines and rules for responsible use.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0013","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-003-2-1-ethical-considerations","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s003","q":"How do you detect potential bias in a set of training texts with a Hugging Face pipeline?","a":"<p>Run each text through a toxicity text-classification pipeline and collect the score and label.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>bias_detector = pipeline(&quot;text-classification&quot;, \n                        model=&quot;unitary/toxic-bert&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0014","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-003-2-1-ethical-considerations","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s003","q":"What does the <code>detect_bias_in_dataset(texts)</code> helper return for each text?","a":"<p>A DataFrame with the <code>text</code>, the <code>bias_score</code> and the <code>label</code> from the classifier.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>results.append({\n    &#x27;text&#x27;: text,\n    &#x27;bias_score&#x27;: result[0][&#x27;score&#x27;],\n    &#x27;label&#x27;: result[0][&#x27;label&#x27;]\n})\nreturn pd.DataFrame(results)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0015","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-003-2-1-ethical-considerations","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s003","q":"How can you add transparency to a model decision with input gradients, and what is the caveat?","a":"<p>Take the gradient of the target class logit with respect to the inputs and pair it with the tokens. It needs a classification model. Token ids are not differentiable in practice, so treat it as a sketch.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>loss = outputs.logits[0, target_class]\nloss.backward()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0016","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-003-2-1-ethical-considerations","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s003","q":"What does the ethical-AI checklist cover for data?","a":"<p>Audit bias, ensure diverse representation, remove PII, and document data origins.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0017","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-003-2-1-ethical-considerations","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s003","q":"What does the ethical-AI checklist cover for transparency, deployment and governance?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Transparency:</strong> model docs, explain decisions, interpretability, regular bias tests.</li>\n  <li><strong>Deployment:</strong> monitor across demographics, feedback loops, retraining, stated limits.</li>\n  <li><strong>Governance:</strong> ethics committee, reviews, compliance, stakeholders.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0018","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-004-2-2-architecture-types-interview-staple","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s004","q":"What are the three LLM architecture types, with an example of each?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><strong>Encoder-only</strong></td><td>BERT</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Decoder-only</strong></td><td>GPT</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Encoder-decoder</strong></td><td>T5, FLAN-T5</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0019","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-004-2-2-architecture-types-interview-staple","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s004","q":"What is an encoder-only model for, what is its training objective and what tasks suit it?","a":"<p>It understands and analyzes input (BERT). The objective is masked language modeling. Typical tasks are sentiment analysis, classification and extractive QA.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0020","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-004-2-2-architecture-types-interview-staple","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s004","q":"What is a decoder-only model for, what is its training objective and what tasks suit it?","a":"<p>It generates text from a prompt (GPT). The objective is autoregressive language modeling. Typical tasks are content creation and writing assistance.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0021","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-004-2-2-architecture-types-interview-staple","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s004","q":"What is an encoder-decoder model for, what is its training objective and what tasks suit it?","a":"<p>It understands <em>and</em> generates (T5, FLAN-T5). The objective is text-to-text. Typical tasks are translation, summarisation and versatile NLP.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0022","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-004-2-2-architecture-types-interview-staple","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s004","q":"How do you load BERT for a two-class sentiment task in Hugging Face?","a":"<p>Load <code>BertForSequenceClassification</code> with <code>num_labels=2</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>tokenizer = BertTokenizer.from_pretrained(&#x27;bert-base-uncased&#x27;)\nmodel = BertForSequenceClassification.from_pretrained(&#x27;bert-base-uncased&#x27;, \n                                                     num_labels=2)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0023","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-004-2-2-architecture-types-interview-staple","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s004","q":"How do you turn BERT's output into negative and positive probabilities?","a":"<p>Apply softmax to the logits, then read index 0 as negative and index 1 as positive.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>predictions = torch.nn.functional.softmax(outputs.logits, dim=-1)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0024","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-004-2-2-architecture-types-interview-staple","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s004","q":"How do you load GPT-2 for text generation and avoid a missing pad token?","a":"<p>Load <code>GPT2LMHeadModel</code> and set the pad token to the end-of-sequence token.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>tokenizer = GPT2Tokenizer.from_pretrained(&#x27;gpt2&#x27;)\nmodel = GPT2LMHeadModel.from_pretrained(&#x27;gpt2&#x27;)\ntokenizer.pad_token = tokenizer.eos_token</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0025","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-004-2-2-architecture-types-interview-staple","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s004","q":"Which <code>model.generate</code> arguments does the GPT-2 example use?","a":"<p><code>max_length</code>, <code>num_return_sequences=1</code>, <code>temperature=0.7</code> and <code>pad_token_id=tokenizer.eos_token_id</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0026","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-005-2-2-architecture-types-interview-staple","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s004","q":"How do you load T5 for conditional generation in Hugging Face?","a":"<p>Use <code>T5ForConditionalGeneration</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>tokenizer = T5Tokenizer.from_pretrained(&#x27;t5-small&#x27;)\nmodel = T5ForConditionalGeneration.from_pretrained(&#x27;t5-small&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0027","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-005-2-2-architecture-types-interview-staple","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s004","q":"How does T5 know which task to perform?","a":"<p>A task prefix in the input text selects the task.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>input_text = f&quot;{task_prefix}: {text}&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0028","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-005-2-2-architecture-types-interview-staple","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s004","q":"Which generation settings does the T5 example use?","a":"<p><code>num_beams=4</code> and <code>early_stopping=True</code>, with <code>max_length</code> passed in (default 150).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0029","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-005-2-2-architecture-types-interview-staple","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s004","q":"How do you call the T5 helper for summarisation and for English to German translation?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>summary = t5_task(&quot;summarize&quot;, text)\ntranslation = t5_task(&quot;translate English to German&quot;, &quot;Hello, how are you?&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0030","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-006-2-3-model-selection-by-task-and-budget","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s005","q":"Which models suit understanding tasks at high, medium and low budget?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Budget</th><th>Model</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>High</td><td>BERT-large or RoBERTa</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Medium</td><td>BERT-base or DistilBERT</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Low</td><td>DistilBERT or TinyBERT</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0031","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-006-2-3-model-selection-by-task-and-budget","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s005","q":"Which models suit generation tasks at high, medium and low budget?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Budget</th><th>Model</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>High</td><td>GPT-3 or GPT-4</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Medium</td><td>GPT-2 or smaller GPT variants</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Low</td><td>DistilGPT-2</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0032","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-006-2-3-model-selection-by-task-and-budget","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s005","q":"Which models suit mixed tasks at high, medium and low budget?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Budget</th><th>Model</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>High</td><td>T5-large or FLAN-T5</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Medium</td><td>T5-base</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Low</td><td>T5-small</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0033","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-006-2-3-model-selection-by-task-and-budget","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s005","q":"What does <code>select_model_architecture</code> return when the task type or budget is unknown?","a":"<p>The string <code>'Consider task-specific fine-tuning'</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>return recommendations.get(task_type, {}).get(computational_budget, &#x27;Consider task-specific fine-tuning&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0034","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-006-2-3-model-selection-by-task-and-budget","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s005","q":"What is the second lecture variant of the model selection function, <code>model_selection_guide</code>, and how does it differ?","a":"<p><code>model_selection_guide</code> has the same shape as the first variant but with extra model names: RoBERTa-large, TinyBERT/MobileBERT, PaLM, FLAN-T5-xl and FLAN-T5-small.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0035","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-006-2-3-model-selection-by-task-and-budget","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s005","q":"What does <code>select_model_architecture('mixed_tasks', 'medium_budget', 'large')</code> recommend?","a":"<p>T5-base.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0036","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-007-2-4-flan-t5-in-focus","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s006","q":"What is instruction tuning, and what does it give FLAN-T5?","a":"<p>The model is trained on many tasks phrased as instructions. FLAN-T5 therefore handles several tasks without task-specific training. It is a text-to-text encoder-decoder available on Hugging Face.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0037","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-007-2-4-flan-t5-in-focus","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s006","q":"What are the FLAN-T5 model sizes in parameters?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Size</th><th>Parameters</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>small</td><td>~80M</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>base</td><td>~250M</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>large</td><td>~780M</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>xl</td><td>~3B</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>xxl</td><td>~11B</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0038","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-007-2-4-flan-t5-in-focus","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s006","q":"What is the rule-of-thumb memory estimate for a model in float32?","a":"<p>4 bytes per parameter, then multiply by 1.5 for activations and batching.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>model_memory_gb = (model_size_params * 4) / (1024**3)\ntotal_memory_gb = model_memory_gb * 1.5</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0039","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-007-2-4-flan-t5-in-focus","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s006","q":"In the memory-estimate helper, what hardware does each total-memory threshold suggest?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>4 GB or less: CPU inference</li>\n  <li>16 GB or less: Consumer GPU</li>\n  <li>80 GB or less: Professional GPU</li>\n  <li>More than 80 GB: Multi-GPU setup required</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0040","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-008-2-4-flan-t5-in-focus","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s006","q":"How does the <code>FlanT5Assistant</code> wrapper load its model, and what is the default?","a":"<p>It loads a tokenizer and a <code>T5ForConditionalGeneration</code> model from a name, with default <code>\"google/flan-t5-base\"</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def __init__(self, model_name=&quot;google/flan-t5-base&quot;):\n    self.tokenizer = T5Tokenizer.from_pretrained(model_name)\n    self.model = T5ForConditionalGeneration.from_pretrained(model_name)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0041","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-008-2-4-flan-t5-in-focus","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s006","q":"How does <code>FlanT5Assistant.process_instruction</code> control randomness?","a":"<p>It takes a <code>temperature</code> (default 0.7) and enables sampling only when it is greater than 0.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>temperature=temperature,\ndo_sample=True if temperature &gt; 0 else False</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0042","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-008-2-4-flan-t5-in-focus","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s006","q":"How does <code>FlanT5Assistant.batch_process</code> handle several instructions?","a":"<p>It loops over them and calls <code>process_instruction</code> for each one, collecting the results.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0043","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-008-2-4-flan-t5-in-focus","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s006","q":"What other prompt wordings work with FLAN-T5?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><code>\"Summarize the following text: {text}\"</code></li>\n  <li><code>\"Translate from {source_lang} to {target_lang}: {text}\"</code></li>\n  <li><code>\"Answer the question based on the context. Context: {context} Question: {question}\"</code></li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0044","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-009-3-1-what-a-prompt-is-and-how-you-talk-to","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s007","q":"What is a prompt?","a":"<p>The instruction (plus context) that sets how the model responds.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0045","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-009-3-1-what-a-prompt-is-and-how-you-talk-to","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s007","q":"What are the ways to talk to an LLM?","a":"<p>Through applications, web interfaces (no code), or direct code integration.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0046","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-009-3-1-what-a-prompt-is-and-how-you-talk-to","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s007","q":"How do you send a prompt to a chat model with the OpenAI client?","a":"<p>Call <code>client.chat.completions.create</code> with a user message.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>response = client.chat.completions.create(\n    model=&quot;gpt-3.5-turbo&quot;,\n    messages=[{&quot;role&quot;: &quot;user&quot;, &quot;content&quot;: &quot;Explain quantum computing&quot;}]\n)\nprint(response.choices[0].message.content)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0047","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-009-3-1-what-a-prompt-is-and-how-you-talk-to","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s007","q":"What does the <code>query_llm</code> helper do, and what is its default model?","a":"<p>It wraps the chat call: it sends the prompt as a user message and returns the reply text. The default model is <code>gpt-3.5-turbo</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def query_llm(prompt, model=&quot;gpt-3.5-turbo&quot;):\n    response = client.chat.completions.create(\n        model=model,\n        messages=[{&quot;role&quot;: &quot;user&quot;, &quot;content&quot;: prompt}]\n    )\n    return response.choices[0].message.content</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0048","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-009-3-1-what-a-prompt-is-and-how-you-talk-to","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s007","q":"What makes a good prompt?","a":"<p>It is clear, concise, specific and contextual.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0049","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-009-3-1-what-a-prompt-is-and-how-you-talk-to","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s007","q":"What is the T5 text-to-text format?","a":"<p>A task keyword prefix tells T5 what to do, followed by the content.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def t5_prompt(task, content):\n    return f&quot;{task}: {content}&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0050","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-009-3-1-what-a-prompt-is-and-how-you-talk-to","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s007","q":"What do the T5 prompts for translate, summarize and question look like?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&quot;translate&quot;: &quot;translate English to French: Hello world&quot;,\n&quot;summarize&quot;: &quot;summarize: Long text content here...&quot;,\n&quot;question&quot;: &quot;question: What is the capital of France?&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0051","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-010-3-2-colab-model-setup","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s008","q":"How do you run the FLAN-T5 notebooks on Colab?","a":"<p>Upload the notebook file and connect a GPU runtime. The free GPU is enough for prototyping.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0052","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-010-3-2-colab-model-setup","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s008","q":"What do <code>TFAutoModel...</code> and <code>Seq2SeqLM</code> mean in <code>TFAutoModelForSeq2SeqLM</code>?","a":"<p><code>TFAutoModel...</code> is the TensorFlow version. <code>Seq2SeqLM</code> is a sequence-to-sequence language model.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0053","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-010-3-2-colab-model-setup","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s008","q":"Are PyTorch to TensorFlow weight-conversion warnings a problem when loading FLAN-T5 in TensorFlow?","a":"<p>No. They are normal.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0054","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-010-3-2-colab-model-setup","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s008","q":"How do you install the libraries and load FLAN-T5-large with TensorFlow?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>!pip install transformers tensorflow\nfrom transformers import TFAutoModelForSeq2SeqLM, AutoTokenizer\ntokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(&quot;google/flan-t5-large&quot;)\nmodel = TFAutoModelForSeq2SeqLM.from_pretrained(&quot;google/flan-t5-large&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0055","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-011-3-3-the-four-steps-every-task-uses-the-s","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s009","q":"What are the four steps of prompting FLAN-T5?","a":"<ol>\n  <li><strong>Define</strong> the prompt (the task prefix matters).</li>\n  <li><strong>Tokenize</strong> it.</li>\n  <li><strong><code>model.generate</code></strong>.</li>\n  <li><strong>Decode</strong> with the tokenizer.</li>\n</ol>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0056","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-011-3-3-the-four-steps-every-task-uses-the-s","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s009","q":"What does <code>return_tensors=\"tf\"</code> do in the tokenizer call?","a":"<p>It returns TensorFlow tensors.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0057","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-011-3-3-the-four-steps-every-task-uses-the-s","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s009","q":"What do <code>max_length=512</code>, <code>truncation=True</code> and <code>padding=True</code> do on the tokenizer?","a":"<p><code>max_length=512</code> is the model's input token limit. <code>truncation=True</code> cuts long inputs. <code>padding=True</code> pads short ones.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0058","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-011-3-3-the-four-steps-every-task-uses-the-s","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s009","q":"What do <code>num_beams=5</code> and <code>early_stopping=True</code> do in <code>model.generate</code>?","a":"<p><code>num_beams=5</code> sets the beam search width. A higher value gives better quality but is slower. <code>early_stopping=True</code> stops when the beams finish.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0059","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-011-3-3-the-four-steps-every-task-uses-the-s","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s009","q":"What does <code>skip_special_tokens=True</code> do when decoding?","a":"<p>It removes special tokens from the decoded text.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0060","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-011-3-3-the-four-steps-every-task-uses-the-s","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s009","q":"What output <code>max_length</code> do summarisation, translation and Q&amp;A use?","a":"<p>Summarise 150, translate 40, QA 50.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0061","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-011-3-3-the-four-steps-every-task-uses-the-s","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s009","q":"What does <code>temperature</code> do, and when does it apply?","a":"<p>It controls randomness (0 = deterministic, 1 = creative). It only applies with <code>do_sample=True</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0062","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-011-3-3-the-four-steps-every-task-uses-the-s","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s009","q":"How do you summarise a text zero-shot with FLAN-T5 in TensorFlow?","a":"<p>Prefix with <code>summarize:</code>, tokenize, generate with <code>max_length=150</code>, and decode. The example output is \"Eat carrots\".</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>inputs = tokenizer(prompt, return_tensors=&quot;tf&quot;, max_length=512, truncation=True, padding=True)\noutputs = model.generate(inputs[&quot;input_ids&quot;], max_length=150, num_beams=5, early_stopping=True)\nprint(tokenizer.decode(outputs[0], skip_special_tokens=True))</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0063","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-011-3-3-the-four-steps-every-task-uses-the-s","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s009","q":"How do you translate English to Spanish with FLAN-T5, and what <code>max_length</code> do you use?","a":"<p>Use the prompt <code>translate English to Spanish: Cheese is delicious.</code> with a shorter <code>max_length=40</code>. The output is \"El queso es delicioso.\"</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>translation_prompt = &quot;translate English to Spanish: Cheese is delicious.&quot;\ntranslation_outputs = model.generate(translation_inputs[&quot;input_ids&quot;], max_length=40, num_beams=5, early_stopping=True)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0064","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-011-3-3-the-four-steps-every-task-uses-the-s","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s009","q":"How do you format a Q&amp;A prompt for FLAN-T5?","a":"<p>Put the context first, then a <code>question:</code> marker and the question. The output for the Great Wall example is \"over 13,000 miles long\".</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>context_question = &quot;The Great Wall of China is over 13,000 miles long. question: How long is the Great Wall of China?&quot;\nquestion_outputs = model.generate(question_inputs[&quot;input_ids&quot;], max_length=50, num_beams=5, early_stopping=True)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0065","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-012-3-4-reusable-helpers","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s010","q":"What does the generic <code>flan_t5_generate</code> helper do?","a":"<p>It tokenizes a prompt, runs <code>model.generate</code> with <code>num_beams=5</code>, and decodes the first output. <code>max_length</code> defaults to 150.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def flan_t5_generate(prompt, max_length=150):\n    return tokenizer.decode(outputs[0], skip_special_tokens=True)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0066","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-012-3-4-reusable-helpers","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s010","q":"How does <code>route_task</code> build the prompt for each task type?","a":"<p>It looks the task up in a dict of prompts and falls back to the raw content.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&quot;summarize&quot;: f&quot;summarize: {content}&quot;,\n&quot;translate&quot;: f&quot;translate English to {kwargs.get(&#x27;target&#x27;, &#x27;French&#x27;)}: {content}&quot;,\n&quot;question&quot;: f&quot;{kwargs.get(&#x27;context&#x27;, &#x27;&#x27;)} question: {content}&quot;,\n&quot;classify&quot;: f&quot;classify sentiment: {content}&quot;,\n&quot;generate&quot;: f&quot;complete: {content}&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0067","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-012-3-4-reusable-helpers","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s010","q":"What is the default target language of <code>route_task</code> for translation?","a":"<p>French, through <code>kwargs.get('target', 'French')</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0068","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-012-3-4-reusable-helpers","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s010","q":"What per-task generation configs does the FLAN-T5 demo <code>handle_task</code> use, and what is hard-coded?","a":"<p>Summarize <code>max_length</code> 150, translate 40, question 50, all with <code>num_beams</code> 5. The default is 100 with 3 beams. The demo <code>handle_task</code> hard-codes Spanish.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0069","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-012-3-4-reusable-helpers","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s010","q":"How does <code>generate_with_params</code> switch between sampling and deterministic output?","a":"<p>It sets <code>do_sample=True</code> only when <code>temperature &gt; 0</code>. The default temperature is 0.7.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def generate_with_params(prompt, num_beams=5, max_length=150, temperature=0.7):</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0070","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-012-3-4-reusable-helpers","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s010","q":"How do you translate one text into several languages with the helpers?","a":"<p>Loop over (source, target) pairs and call <code>translate_text</code>, which uses <code>max_length=40</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def translate_text(text, source_lang=&quot;English&quot;, target_lang=&quot;French&quot;):\n    prompt = f&quot;translate {source_lang} to {target_lang}: {text}&quot;\n    return flan_t5_generate(prompt, max_length=40)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0071","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-013-3-4-reusable-helpers","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s010","q":"What does true batched generation do, and why is it better than looping?","a":"<p>It tokenizes a list of prompts at once and generates for all of them. That is better than looping one prompt at a time.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>inputs = tokenizer(batch, return_tensors=&quot;tf&quot;, padding=True, \n                  truncation=True, max_length=512)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0072","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-013-3-4-reusable-helpers","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s010","q":"Which settings does the <code>batch_process</code> helper use for generation?","a":"<p>A default <code>batch_size=4</code>, <code>max_length=150</code> and <code>num_beams=3</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0073","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-013-3-4-reusable-helpers","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s010","q":"What does the <code>FlanT5Processor</code> class wrapper do?","a":"<p>It loads FLAN-T5-large, builds the prompt per task, and picks <code>max_length</code> per task.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>max_len = {&quot;summarize&quot;: 150, &quot;translate&quot;: 40, &quot;question&quot;: 50}.get(task, 100)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0074","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-013-3-4-reusable-helpers","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s010","q":"What prompt does <code>FlanT5Processor</code> build for each task?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>return f&quot;summarize: {content}&quot;\nreturn f&quot;translate English to Spanish: {content}&quot;\nreturn f&quot;{context} question: {content}&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0075","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-014-3-5-robustness-validation-speed","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s011","q":"How do you make FLAN-T5 faster or lighter in production?","a":"<p>Use a smaller model (<code>flan-t5-base</code>). Reduce input <code>max_length</code> (256), output <code>max_length</code> and <code>num_beams</code> (3) to save memory.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0076","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-014-3-5-robustness-validation-speed","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s011","q":"What settings does <code>memory_efficient_generate</code> use?","a":"<p>Input <code>max_length=256</code>, output <code>max_length=100</code> and <code>num_beams=3</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>inputs = tokenizer(prompt, return_tensors=&quot;tf&quot;, max_length=256, truncation=True)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0077","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-014-3-5-robustness-validation-speed","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s011","q":"How does <code>robust_prompt_execution</code> handle failures?","a":"<p>It retries up to <code>max_retries</code> (default 3) and returns an error message after the last failed attempt. It returns <code>None</code> if no response passes validation.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>return f&quot;Error after {max_retries} attempts: {str(e)}&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0078","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-014-3-5-robustness-validation-speed","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s011","q":"What does <code>validate_response</code> check?","a":"<p>That the response is not empty and has non-blank text.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>return response and len(response.strip()) &gt; 0</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0079","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-014-3-5-robustness-validation-speed","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s011","q":"What per-task rules does <code>validate_output</code> apply?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&quot;summarize&quot;: lambda x: len(x.split()) &lt; 50,\n&quot;translate&quot;: lambda x: len(x) &gt; 0 and not x.startswith(&quot;translate&quot;),\n&quot;question&quot;: lambda x: len(x.split()) &lt; 20</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0080","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-014-3-5-robustness-validation-speed","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s011","q":"What checks does the <code>quality_check</code> heuristic run?","a":"<p>Length (non-empty output), relevance (the task name appears in the output, except for <code>question</code>), and completeness (output does not end with \"...\").</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0081","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-015-4-prompt-engineering-patterns","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s012","q":"What are the four reminders for prompt engineering with T5?","a":"<p>Always use task-specific prefixes with T5, set <code>max_length</code> per task, validate outputs, and batch when you can.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0082","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-016-4-1-core-patterns","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s013","q":"What are the core prompt engineering patterns?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Pattern</th><th>Idea</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><strong>Few-shot</strong></td><td>Give worked examples before the real task</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Cognitive verifier</strong></td><td>Model first asks clarifying questions, then answers using all your replies</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Question refinement</strong></td><td>Model suggests a better version of your question and asks if you want to use it</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Gameplay</strong></td><td>Turn learning into a game with rules</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Chain of thought</strong></td><td>Ask for step-by-step reasoning</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Role-based</strong></td><td>\"You are a {role}...\"</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0083","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-016-4-1-core-patterns","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s013","q":"How do you build a few-shot prompt from examples?","a":"<p>Add each example as Input/Output, then end with the new input and an empty <code>Output:</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>prompt += f&quot;Input: {example[&#x27;input&#x27;]}\\nOutput: {example[&#x27;output&#x27;]}\\n\\n&quot;\nprompt += f&quot;Input: {new_task}\\nOutput:&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0084","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-016-4-1-core-patterns","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s013","q":"What system prompt implements the cognitive verifier pattern?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>system_prompt = &quot;&quot;&quot;Whenever I ask a question, only ask me for additional \ninformation to clarify what I&#x27;m asking before providing a final answer. \nPlease combine all my responses.&quot;&quot;&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0085","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-016-4-1-core-patterns","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s013","q":"What system prompt implements the question refinement pattern?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>system_prompt = &quot;&quot;&quot;When I ask a question, suggest a better question \nand ask me if I would like to use it instead.&quot;&quot;&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0086","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-016-4-1-core-patterns","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s013","q":"What prompt implements the gameplay pattern?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>return f&quot;Create a game for me around {topic}. Give fundamental rules of the game.&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0087","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-016-4-1-core-patterns","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s013","q":"How do you write a chain-of-thought prompt?","a":"<p>Ask the model to solve the problem step by step and start the numbered list.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>return f&quot;&quot;&quot;Solve this step by step:\nLet&#x27;s think through this step by step:\n1.&quot;&quot;&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0088","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-016-4-1-core-patterns","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s013","q":"What does the FLAN-T5 flavour of chain of thought look like?","a":"<p>It is just <code>f\"solve step by step: {problem}\"</code> with <code>max_length=200</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0089","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-016-4-1-core-patterns","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s013","q":"How do you write a role-based prompt?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>return f&quot;You are a {role}. {task}&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0090","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-016-4-1-core-patterns","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s013","q":"How does <code>combine_patterns</code> combine few-shot with chain of thought?","a":"<p>It appends <code>Let's think step by step:</code> to a few-shot prompt.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>return f&quot;{few_shot_prompt([], content)}\\nLet&#x27;s think step by step:&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0091","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-017-4-2-templates-and-context-management","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s014","q":"How does a <code>PromptTemplate</code> class work?","a":"<p>It stores a template string and fills it with <code>str.format</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def format(self, **kwargs):\n    return self.template.format(**kwargs)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0092","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-017-4-2-templates-and-context-management","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s014","q":"Which prompt templates does the <code>PromptTemplate</code> templates dict hold for translation, summary and code generation?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&quot;translation&quot;: &quot;Translate from {source} to {target}: {text}&quot;,\n&quot;summary&quot;: &quot;Summarize the following in {length} words: {text}&quot;,\n&quot;code_gen&quot;: &quot;Write a {language} function that {description}&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0093","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-017-4-2-templates-and-context-management","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s014","q":"How does <code>manage_context</code> handle a conversation that exceeds the context window?","a":"<p>It keeps the system message and the most recent turns when the token count passes <code>max_tokens</code> (default 4000).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>return [messages[0]] + messages[-(max_tokens//100):]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0094","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-018-5-few-shot-in-context-learning","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s015","q":"What is few-shot learning?","a":"<p>Putting worked examples in the prompt so the model learns the task format and output style.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0095","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-018-5-few-shot-in-context-learning","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s015","q":"What is in-context learning (ICL)?","a":"<p>Essentially the same technique as few-shot learning.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0096","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-018-5-few-shot-in-context-learning","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s015","q":"Do weights change in few-shot or in-context learning?","a":"<p>No. Weights do not change, which contrasts with transfer learning and fine-tuning.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0097","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-018-5-few-shot-in-context-learning","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s015","q":"What are the rules of thumb for writing few-shot examples?","a":"<p>Use 2–3 high-quality examples, separated by blank lines, matching the desired output format. Mind the 512-token input limit.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0098","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-018-5-few-shot-in-context-learning","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s015","q":"Which models does few-shot learning help most?","a":"<p>Smaller models. It works across tasks.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0099","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-019-5-1-notebook-few-shot-summarisation-tran","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s016","q":"How do you combine few-shot examples with the new prompt in the FLAN-T5 notebook?","a":"<p>Join the examples and the new prompt with blank lines.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>combined_prompt = &quot;\\n\\n&quot;.join(few_shot_examples + [prompt])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0100","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-019-5-1-notebook-few-shot-summarisation-tran","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s016","q":"How does few-shot summarisation change the output compared with zero-shot?","a":"<p>The summary is fuller and better formatted, for example \"Carrots are a great source of vitamin A, which is crucial for maintaining healthy eyesight.\"</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0101","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-019-5-1-notebook-few-shot-summarisation-tran","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s016","q":"What is the format of a few-shot translation example for FLAN-T5?","a":"<p>The instruction, the English text, then <code>Translation:</code> with the Spanish text.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&quot;translate English to Spanish: &#x27;The cat sits on the mat.&#x27; Translation: &#x27;El gato se sienta en la alfombra.&#x27;&quot;,</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0102","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-019-5-1-notebook-few-shot-summarisation-tran","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s016","q":"What <code>max_length</code> does the few-shot translation use?","a":"<p>40.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>translation_outputs = model.generate(translation_inputs[&quot;input_ids&quot;], max_length=40, num_beams=5, early_stopping=True)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0103","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-019-5-1-notebook-few-shot-summarisation-tran","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s016","q":"What is the format of a few-shot Q&amp;A example for FLAN-T5?","a":"<p>The context sentence, then <code>question:</code> and <code>answer:</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&quot;The capital of France is Paris. question: &#x27;What is the capital of France?&#x27; answer: &#x27;The capital of France is Paris.&#x27;&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0104","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-019-5-1-notebook-few-shot-summarisation-tran","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s016","q":"What <code>max_length</code> does the few-shot Q&amp;A use, and what is the answer to the Mount Everest question?","a":"<p><code>max_length=50</code>. The answer is \"Mount Everest\".</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>question_outputs = model.generate(question_inputs[&quot;input_ids&quot;], max_length=50, num_beams=5, early_stopping=True)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0105","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-019-5-1-notebook-few-shot-summarisation-tran","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s016","q":"What is the lecture variant of few-shot example blocks?","a":"<p>Blocks like <code>\"summarize: &lt;text&gt;\\n&lt;summary&gt;\"</code> or <code>\"&lt;context&gt; question: &lt;q&gt;\\n&lt;answer&gt;\"</code>, separated by blank lines.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0106","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-020-5-2-generic-few-shot-tooling","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s017","q":"What does <code>create_few_shot_prompt</code> build?","a":"<p>A prompt with each example as <code>task_type: input</code> then the output, followed by <code>task_type: new_input</code> for the new case.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>example_str += f&quot;{task_type}: {ex[&#x27;input&#x27;]}\\n{ex[&#x27;output&#x27;]}\\n\\n&quot;\nfull_prompt = f&quot;{example_str}{task_type}: {new_input}&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0107","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-020-5-2-generic-few-shot-tooling","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s017","q":"What does dynamic example selection do, and what is the lecture stub's limit?","a":"<p>It picks the most relevant examples for the new input. The stub just slices the pool. In practice use similarity metrics.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>selected = example_pool[:num_examples]  # In practice, use similarity metrics</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0108","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-020-5-2-generic-few-shot-tooling","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s017","q":"What is the default number of examples in <code>select_best_examples</code>?","a":"<p><code>num_examples=2</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0109","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-021-5-2-generic-few-shot-tooling","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s017","q":"What does <code>validate_examples</code> enforce for few-shot examples?","a":"<p>It keeps examples whose input is longer than 10 characters and whose output is non-empty, and returns at most 3. The summarize and translate checks are written in, but the final <code>else</code> appends every example, so they remove nothing.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>return valid_examples[:3]  # Limit to 3 best examples</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0110","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-021-5-2-generic-few-shot-tooling","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s017","q":"How does <code>optimize_prompt_length</code> control prompt length?","a":"<p>It estimates tokens as characters divided by 4 and keeps only the first example if the estimate exceeds <code>max_tokens</code> (default 400).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>estimated_tokens = len(prompt) // 4\nreduced_examples = examples[:1]  # Keep only best example</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0111","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-021-5-2-generic-few-shot-tooling","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s017","q":"How do you compare zero-shot and few-shot output side by side?","a":"<p>Build both prompts, generate both, and return them with an improvement flag.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>zero_shot_prompt = f&quot;{task_type}: {input_text}&quot;\n&quot;improvement&quot;: len(few_shot_result) &gt; len(zero_shot_result)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0112","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-022-6-prompt-engineering-case-studies","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s018","q":"What is the common thread of the prompt engineering case studies?","a":"<p>Replace a <strong>generic</strong> prompt with a <strong>specific, contextual, structured</strong> one that guides the user or model.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0113","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-022-6-prompt-engineering-case-studies","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s018","q":"What was the customer service (Zendesk, Salesforce) prompt problem and fix?","a":"<p>A generic greeting led to meandering conversations. Categorised options route users to the right channel. The result is faster routing and better satisfaction.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0114","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-022-6-prompt-engineering-case-studies","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s018","q":"What was the healthcare (IBM Watson) prompt problem and fix?","a":"<p>Vague prompts gave ambiguous diagnostic help. A structured request for symptoms, tests, history, and duration/severity gave more accurate, actionable insights.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0115","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-022-6-prompt-engineering-case-studies","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s018","q":"What was the media (Google News) prompt problem and fix?","a":"<p>Summaries were misleading and missed critical points. Asking for key points, controversies and implications gave balanced, more accurate digests.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0116","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-022-6-prompt-engineering-case-studies","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s018","q":"What was the education (Duolingo) prompt problem and fix?","a":"<p>Plain translation prompts were mechanical with low engagement. Adding a scenario, such as explaining to a friend in a Paris cafe, gave higher engagement and more relatable output.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0117","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-022-6-prompt-engineering-case-studies","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s018","q":"How does the customer service prompt route users?","a":"<p>It lists categorised options and asks which one applies.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>1. Account issue\n2. Technical support  \n3. Billing inquiry</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0118","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-022-6-prompt-engineering-case-studies","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s018","q":"What four items does the medical prompt ask the user for?","a":"<p>Symptoms in detail, recent medical tests and results, relevant medical history, and duration and severity of symptoms.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0119","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-022-6-prompt-engineering-case-studies","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s018","q":"How does <code>watson_medical_query</code> structure its request?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>prompt = f&quot;&quot;&quot;Medical Analysis Request:\nSymptoms: {symptoms}\nRecent Tests: {tests}\nMedical History: {history}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0120","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-023-6-prompt-engineering-case-studies","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s018","q":"What does the news summary prompt ask the model to focus on?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Main facts and developments</li>\n  <li>Any controversies or opposing viewpoints</li>\n  <li>Implications and significance</li>\n  <li>Critical details that impact understanding</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0121","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-023-6-prompt-engineering-case-studies","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s018","q":"What does <code>enhanced_news_digest</code> return for each article?","a":"<p>A dict with the <code>title</code>, the <code>summary</code> and the <code>source</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>summaries.append({\n    &#x27;title&#x27;: article[&#x27;title&#x27;],\n    &#x27;summary&#x27;: summary,\n    &#x27;source&#x27;: article[&#x27;source&#x27;]\n})</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0122","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-023-6-prompt-engineering-case-studies","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s018","q":"How does the contextual translation prompt add a scenario?","a":"<p>It asks for the translation as if you were in a context and requests a natural, conversational translation that fits the scenario.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>return f&quot;&quot;&quot;Translate the following sentence as if you were {context}:</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0123","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-023-6-prompt-engineering-case-studies","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s018","q":"What is the default context of <code>duolingo_exercise</code>?","a":"<p><code>\"explaining it to a friend in a cafe in Paris\"</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def duolingo_exercise(sentence, context=&quot;explaining it to a friend in a cafe in Paris&quot;):</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0124","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-023-6-prompt-engineering-case-studies","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s018","q":"What is the generic prompt versus the optimised prompt for translation?","a":"<p>Generic: <code>\"Translate: {input}\"</code> (vague, low engagement). Optimised: <code>\"Translate '{input}' as if explaining to a friend in a casual conversation\"</code> (specific, contextual, engaging).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0125","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-023-6-prompt-engineering-case-studies","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s018","q":"Which metrics does each case-study domain track?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Metrics</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Customer service</td><td>Resolution time, satisfaction, escalation rate</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Healthcare</td><td>Accuracy, actionability, confidence</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Media</td><td>Completeness, accuracy, readability</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Education</td><td>Engagement, retention, satisfaction</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0126","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-024-6-prompt-engineering-case-studies","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s018","q":"What is the industry prompt-template bank?","a":"<p>A function that returns a template by industry and task type, for customer service, healthcare, media and education.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>return templates.get(industry, {}).get(task_type, &quot;Generic template for {industry} {task_type}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0127","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-024-6-prompt-engineering-case-studies","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s018","q":"Which task types does each industry have in the template bank?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Industry</th><th>Task types</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>customer_service</td><td>greeting, routing, resolution</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>healthcare</td><td>intake, analysis, follow_up</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>media</td><td>summary, analysis, digest</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>education</td><td>translation, explanation, practice</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0128","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-024-6-prompt-engineering-case-studies","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s018","q":"What generic checks does <code>validate_prompt_quality</code> run?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&#x27;specificity&#x27;: len(prompt.split()) &gt; 10,\n&#x27;clarity&#x27;: &#x27;?&#x27; in prompt or &#x27;please&#x27; in prompt.lower(),\n&#x27;context&#x27;: any(word in prompt.lower() for word in [&#x27;describe&#x27;, &#x27;provide&#x27;, &#x27;specify&#x27;]),\n&#x27;actionability&#x27;: any(word in prompt.lower() for word in [&#x27;select&#x27;, &#x27;choose&#x27;, &#x27;tell&#x27;])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0129","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-024-6-prompt-engineering-case-studies","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s018","q":"What domain-specific keyword does <code>validate_prompt_quality</code> look for in each domain?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>customer_service: <code>options</code></li>\n  <li>healthcare: <code>symptoms</code></li>\n  <li>media: <code>summarize</code></li>\n  <li>education: <code>translate</code> or <code>explain</code></li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0130","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-024-6-prompt-engineering-case-studies","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s018","q":"How is the prompt quality score computed?","a":"<p>As the fraction of checks that passed.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&#x27;score&#x27;: sum(quality_checks.values()) / len(quality_checks),</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0131","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-024-6-prompt-engineering-case-studies","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s018","q":"What suggestions does <code>get_improvement_suggestions</code> give?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Specificity fails: add more specific details and requirements.</li>\n  <li>Clarity fails: include clear questions or instructions.</li>\n  <li>Context fails: provide more contextual guidance.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0132","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-025-6-prompt-engineering-case-studies","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s018","q":"How does <code>ab_test_prompts</code> pick the winning prompt?","a":"<p>It scores both prompts on every test case, averages the scores, and picks the higher average.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>winner = &#x27;prompt_a&#x27; if results[&#x27;prompt_a&#x27;][&#x27;avg&#x27;] &gt; results[&#x27;prompt_b&#x27;][&#x27;avg&#x27;] else &#x27;prompt_b&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0133","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-025-6-prompt-engineering-case-studies","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s018","q":"What does <code>ab_test_prompts</code> report as the improvement?","a":"<p>The absolute difference between the two averages.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&#x27;improvement&#x27;: abs(results[&#x27;prompt_a&#x27;][&#x27;avg&#x27;] - results[&#x27;prompt_b&#x27;][&#x27;avg&#x27;])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0134","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-025-6-prompt-engineering-case-studies","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s018","q":"What is the rollout loop for prompt improvement?","a":"<p>Analyse current prompt performance → identify pain points and user needs → design contextual, specific prompts → A/B test against current → measure impact on key metrics → iterate.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0135","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-026-7-challenge-few-shot-article-translation","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s019","q":"What is the task of the few-shot article translation challenge?","a":"<p>Build a few-shot prompt that translates English articles to Spanish while preserving context. It uses CNN/DailyMail and FLAN-T5-large (<code>flan-t5-small</code> if GPU-limited).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0136","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-026-7-challenge-few-shot-article-translation","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s019","q":"Why is long-article few-shot translation a problem for FLAN-T5, and what does the challenge use?","a":"<p>Long articles plus examples can exceed the 512-token window. The challenge uses two examples and output <code>max_length=500</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0137","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-026-7-challenge-few-shot-article-translation","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s019","q":"How do you load the CNN/DailyMail dataset in the challenge?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from datasets import load_dataset\ndataset = load_dataset(&#x27;abisee/cnn_dailymail&#x27;, &#x27;3.0.0&#x27;)\nprint(dataset[&#x27;train&#x27;][0])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0138","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-026-7-challenge-few-shot-article-translation","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s019","q":"Which libraries does the few-shot translation challenge install?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>!pip install transformers tensorflow datasets</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0139","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-026-7-challenge-few-shot-article-translation","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s019","q":"How are the few-shot article examples stored in the challenge?","a":"<p>As a list of dicts with an <code>article</code> and its manual <code>translation</code>. Each article has ~200-word English/Spanish pairs for three articles.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0140","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-027-7-challenge-few-shot-article-translation","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s019","q":"In the few-shot article translation challenge, how do you build the few-shot prompt from the first two entries of the <code>articles</code> list?","a":"<p>Loop over <code>articles[:2]</code> and append the instruction, the text and the translation.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>for example in articles[:2]:\n    few_shot_prompt += f&quot;Translate this text from English to Spanish:\\n\\n Text: \\n\\n {example[&#x27;article&#x27;]} \\n\\n Translation: \\n\\n {example[&#x27;translation&#x27;]} \\n\\n &quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0141","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-027-7-challenge-few-shot-article-translation","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s019","q":"How do you add the new article to the few-shot translation prompt?","a":"<p>Take a test article and append it with an empty <code>Translation:</code> at the end.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>new_article = dataset[&#x27;test&#x27;][0][&#x27;article&#x27;]\nprompt_with_new_article = few_shot_prompt + f&quot;\\n Translate this text from English to Spanish: \\n\\n Text: \\n\\n {new_article} \\n\\n Translation: &quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0142","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-027-7-challenge-few-shot-article-translation","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s019","q":"How do you generate the translation for the challenge prompt?","a":"<p>Tokenize the prompt, call <code>model.generate</code> with <code>max_length=500</code>, and decode.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>inputs = tokenizer(prompt_with_new_article, return_tensors=&quot;tf&quot;)\noutputs = model.generate(inputs[&quot;input_ids&quot;], max_length=500)\ntranslation = tokenizer.decode(outputs[0], skip_special_tokens=True)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0143","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-027-7-challenge-few-shot-article-translation","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s019","q":"How do you evaluate the few-shot article translation, and what if context is lost?","a":"<p>Compare <code>new_article</code> with <code>translation</code>. If context is lost, add more detailed examples or reword the instruction.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0144","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-028-7-challenge-few-shot-article-translation","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s019","q":"How does <code>prepare_translation_examples</code> build example pairs?","a":"<p>It summarises each article first (for GPU efficiency), then translates the summary into Spanish.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>summary_prompt = f&quot;summarize: {article}&quot;\n&#x27;spanish&#x27;: translate_text(summary)  # Pre-translated examples</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0145","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-028-7-challenge-few-shot-article-translation","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s019","q":"What does the <code>translate_text</code> helper do for creating example translations?","a":"<p>It uses the prompt <code>translate English to Spanish: {text}</code> and generates with <code>max_length=200</code> and <code>num_beams=5</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0146","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-028-7-challenge-few-shot-article-translation","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s019","q":"How does <code>create_translation_prompt</code> lay out the few-shot translation prompt?","a":"<p>It starts with the instruction, then lists <code>Text:</code> and <code>Translation:</code> for each example, and ends with the new text and an empty <code>Translation:</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>prompt = &quot;translate this text from English to Spanish:\\n\\n&quot;\nprompt += f&quot;Text: {new_text}\\n&quot;\nprompt += &quot;Translation:&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0147","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-028-7-challenge-few-shot-article-translation","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s019","q":"What does <code>few_shot_translate</code> do, and what is its default output length?","a":"<p>It builds the few-shot prompt, tokenizes and generates. The default <code>max_length</code> is 500 with <code>num_beams=5</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def few_shot_translate(text, examples, max_length=500):</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0148","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-029-7-challenge-few-shot-article-translation","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s019","q":"What does the context-aware translation prompt add to each example?","a":"<p>A note on the tone to preserve.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>prompt += f&quot;Context preserved: {example[&#x27;context_note&#x27;]}\\n\\n&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0149","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-029-7-challenge-few-shot-article-translation","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s019","q":"What context notes do the enhanced examples use?","a":"<p><code>\"Formal business context maintained\"</code> for a meeting sentence and <code>\"Casual tone preserved\"</code> for \"Hey, what's up?\".</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0150","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-029-7-challenge-few-shot-article-translation","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s019","q":"What does <code>multimodal_translation_pipeline</code> do?","a":"<p>It is a cross-task pipeline. Step 1 summarises a long article. Step 2 translates the summary with <code>few_shot_translate</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>translation = few_shot_translate(summary, examples)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0151","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-029-7-challenge-few-shot-article-translation","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s019","q":"How does <code>optimize_for_limited_gpu</code> adapt the pipeline for a small GPU?","a":"<p>It loads <code>google/flan-t5-small</code>, uses input <code>max_length=256</code>, output <code>max_length=200</code> and <code>num_beams=3</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>small_tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(&quot;google/flan-t5-small&quot;)\nsmall_model = TFAutoModelForSeq2SeqLM.from_pretrained(&quot;google/flan-t5-small&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0152","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-029-7-challenge-few-shot-article-translation","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s019","q":"What heuristic checks does <code>validate_translation</code> run?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&#x27;non_empty&#x27;: len(translation.strip()) &gt; 0,\n&#x27;different_from_original&#x27;: translation.lower() != original.lower(),\n&#x27;appropriate_length&#x27;: 0.3 &lt;= len(translation)/len(original) &lt;= 2.0,</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0153","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-029-7-challenge-few-shot-article-translation","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s019","q":"How does <code>validate_translation</code> use <code>expected_elements</code>?","a":"<p>It checks that at least one expected element appears in the translation, ignoring case.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0154","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-030-8-transfer-learning-vs-fine-tuning","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s020","q":"What is the difference between transfer learning and fine-tuning?","a":"<p>Transfer learning uses a pre-trained model plus a new task-specific head and keeps the base mostly <strong>frozen</strong>. Fine-tuning updates <strong>all</strong> weights and biases on the new dataset.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0155","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-030-8-transfer-learning-vs-fine-tuning","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s020","q":"What is the chef analogy for transfer learning vs fine-tuning?","a":"<p>Transfer learning is a chef adapting existing skills to a new kitchen. Fine-tuning is a chef learning an entirely new cuisine.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0156","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-030-8-transfer-learning-vs-fine-tuning","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s020","q":"When do you use transfer learning, and when fine-tuning?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th></th><th>Use when</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><strong>Transfer learning</strong></td><td>Similar tasks, little data/compute, quick adaptation, prototyping</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Fine-tuning</strong></td><td>Different task/domain shift, large dataset, maximum accuracy, specialised domain</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0157","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-030-8-transfer-learning-vs-fine-tuning","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s020","q":"What approach does transfer learning take, and what approach does fine-tuning take?","a":"<p>Transfer learning keeps the structure intact and trains only new components. Fine-tuning further trains the whole model.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0158","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-030-8-transfer-learning-vs-fine-tuning","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s020","q":"What decision rule picks a transfer strategy?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>High task similarity and small data: frozen transfer.</li>\n  <li>Medium similarity and high compute: progressive fine-tuning.</li>\n  <li>Low similarity and large data: full fine-tuning.</li>\n  <li>Otherwise: partial transfer.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>if task_similarity == &#x27;high&#x27; and data_size == &#x27;small&#x27;:\n    return &#x27;transfer_learning_frozen&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0159","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-030-8-transfer-learning-vs-fine-tuning","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s020","q":"What are the success factors for transfer learning and fine-tuning?","a":"<p>A model pre-trained on a similar domain, freezing according to task similarity, a lower learning rate when fine-tuning, starting frozen and unfreezing gradually, quality labelled data, and comparing against a baseline.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0160","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-031-8-1-generic-freeze-the-base-pattern-kera","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s021","q":"How do you freeze a base model in the generic Keras transfer learning pattern?","a":"<p>Set <code>base_model.trainable = not freeze_base</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def create_transfer_model(base_model, num_classes, freeze_base=True):\n    base_model.trainable = not freeze_base</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0161","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-031-8-1-generic-freeze-the-base-pattern-kera","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s021","q":"What layers does the generic transfer model add on top of the base?","a":"<p>Global average pooling and a softmax Dense layer for the classes.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>tf.keras.layers.GlobalAveragePooling2D(),\ntf.keras.layers.Dense(num_classes, activation=&#x27;softmax&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0162","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-032-8-2-lecture-examples-across-domains","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s022","q":"How is VGG-19 used for pneumonia detection with transfer learning?","a":"<p>ImageNet features such as edges and textures transfer to small medical datasets. Load VGG19 without the top, add a head, and freeze the base for binary classification.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>base_model = VGG19(weights=&#x27;imagenet&#x27;, include_top=False, input_shape=(224, 224, 3))</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0163","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-032-8-2-lecture-examples-across-domains","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s022","q":"What head and compile settings does the VGG-19 pneumonia model use?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>tf.keras.layers.Flatten(),\ntf.keras.layers.Dense(128, activation=&#x27;relu&#x27;),\ntf.keras.layers.Dense(1, activation=&#x27;sigmoid&#x27;)  # Binary classification\nloss=&#x27;binary_crossentropy&#x27;,</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0164","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-032-8-2-lecture-examples-across-domains","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s022","q":"How is the regularised medical classifier different from the first VGG-19 model?","a":"<p>It uses global pooling and dropout.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>tf.keras.layers.GlobalAveragePooling2D(),\ntf.keras.layers.Dropout(0.5),\ntf.keras.layers.Dense(512, activation=&#x27;relu&#x27;),\ntf.keras.layers.Dropout(0.3),</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0165","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-032-8-2-lecture-examples-across-domains","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s022","q":"How do you load BERT for sentiment classification with TensorFlow?","a":"<p>BERT is pre-trained on a large corpus and works well with limited review data.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>model = TFBertForSequenceClassification.from_pretrained(&#x27;bert-base-uncased&#x27;, num_labels=2)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0166","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-032-8-2-lecture-examples-across-domains","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s022","q":"What loss does the BERT sentiment example compile with?","a":"<p><code>sparse_categorical_crossentropy</code>, with <code>optimizer='adam'</code> and <code>metrics=['accuracy']</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0167","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-032-8-2-lecture-examples-across-domains","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s022","q":"How does <code>tokenize_reviews</code> prepare product reviews for a TensorFlow BERT classifier?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>return tokenizer(reviews, truncation=True, padding=True, \n                max_length=max_length, return_tensors=&#x27;tf&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0168","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-033-8-2-lecture-examples-across-domains","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s022","q":"Why is MobileNet used for plant disease detection?","a":"<p>It is built for mobile and embedded use, and balances accuracy and efficiency.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0169","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-033-8-2-lecture-examples-across-domains","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s022","q":"What head and loss does the MobileNet plant disease model use?","a":"<p>Global average pooling, a Dense 128 relu layer and a Dense 10 softmax layer (10 plant diseases), with <code>categorical_crossentropy</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>tf.keras.layers.Dense(10, activation=&#x27;softmax&#x27;)  # 10 plant diseases</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0170","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-033-8-2-lecture-examples-across-domains","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s022","q":"Which pre-trained models does <code>select_transfer_model</code> recommend for image classification?","a":"<p>ResNet50 for large data, MobileNet for small data, and VGG19 for medical.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0171","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-033-8-2-lecture-examples-across-domains","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s022","q":"Which pre-trained models does <code>select_transfer_model</code> recommend for text classification?","a":"<p>BERT for general, DistilBERT for lightweight, and mBERT for multilingual.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0172","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-033-8-2-lecture-examples-across-domains","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s022","q":"Which pre-trained models does <code>select_transfer_model</code> recommend for object detection?","a":"<p>EfficientDet for accuracy-focused, YOLO for speed-focused, and MobileNet-SSD for mobile.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0173","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-033-8-2-lecture-examples-across-domains","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s022","q":"What does <code>select_transfer_model</code> return when nothing matches?","a":"<p><code>'BERT'</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>return models.get(task_type, {}).get(data_size, &#x27;BERT&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0174","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-034-8-3-progressive-fine-tuning-frozen-first","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s023","q":"What are the two phases of progressive fine-tuning?","a":"<p>Phase 1 trains only the new layers for 5 epochs. Phase 2 unfreezes the base model and fine-tunes at a lower learning rate for 3 epochs.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0175","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-034-8-3-progressive-fine-tuning-frozen-first","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s023","q":"How do you unfreeze the base model and lower the learning rate in progressive fine-tuning?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>model.layers[0].trainable = True  # Unfreeze base model\noptimizer=tf.keras.optimizers.Adam(1e-5),  # Lower learning rate</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0176","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-034-8-3-progressive-fine-tuning-frozen-first","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s023","q":"What must you do after changing <code>trainable</code> in Keras?","a":"<p><strong>Recompile</strong> the model.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0177","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-035-8-4-deployment-and-evaluation-helpers","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s024","q":"How do you shrink a Keras model for speed with TensorFlow Lite?","a":"<p>Convert it with <code>TFLiteConverter</code> and the default optimisation.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>converter = tf.lite.TFLiteConverter.from_keras_model(model)\nconverter.optimizations = [tf.lite.Optimize.DEFAULT]\ntflite_model = converter.convert()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0178","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-035-8-4-deployment-and-evaluation-helpers","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s024","q":"How do you shrink a Keras model for memory with TensorFlow Lite?","a":"<p>Use <code>OPTIMIZE_FOR_SIZE</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>converter.optimizations = [tf.lite.Optimize.OPTIMIZE_FOR_SIZE]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0179","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-035-8-4-deployment-and-evaluation-helpers","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s024","q":"How does <code>evaluate_transfer_learning</code> measure the gain over a baseline?","a":"<p>It subtracts the baseline accuracy from the test accuracy and reports the percentage improvement.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>results[&#x27;improvement&#x27;] = test_accuracy - baseline_accuracy\nresults[&#x27;improvement_percentage&#x27;] = (results[&#x27;improvement&#x27;] / baseline_accuracy) * 100</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0180","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-036-9-transfer-learning-on-flan-t5-en-es-tra","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s025","q":"What is the goal of the Chapter 3 demos with FLAN-T5?","a":"<p>Fine-tune FLAN-T5-base for English→Spanish translation on the Hugging Face dataset <strong><code>Helsinki-NLP/opus-100</code></strong> (<code>en-es</code>), training only the head and freezing the pre-trained layers.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0181","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-036-9-transfer-learning-on-flan-t5-en-es-tra","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s025","q":"Which notebooks cover transfer learning on FLAN-T5?","a":"<p><code>Chapter3_Demo1_TransferLearning</code> and <code>Chapter3_Demo2_Translation_FlanT5_with_Evaluation</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0182","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-037-9-1-load-preprocess-convert","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s026","q":"How do you load FLAN-T5-base and the opus-100 en-es dataset?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(&quot;google/flan-t5-base&quot;)\nmodel = TFAutoModelForSeq2SeqLM.from_pretrained(&quot;google/flan-t5-base&quot;)\ndataset = load_dataset(&#x27;Helsinki-NLP/opus-100&#x27;, &#x27;en-es&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0183","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-037-9-1-load-preprocess-convert","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s026","q":"What does seq2seq preprocessing do for FLAN-T5 translation?","a":"<p>It prefixes the task, tokenizes inputs, tokenizes targets as <code>labels</code>, and also supplies <code>decoder_input_ids</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>inputs = [f&#x27;Translate from English to Spanish: {example[&quot;en&quot;]}&#x27; for example in examples[&#x27;translation&#x27;]]\ntargets = [example[&#x27;es&#x27;] for example in examples[&#x27;translation&#x27;]]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0184","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-037-9-1-load-preprocess-convert","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s026","q":"Which tokenizer settings does the preprocessing use?","a":"<p><code>max_length=128</code>, <code>truncation=True</code> and <code>padding=\"max_length\"</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0185","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-037-9-1-load-preprocess-convert","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s026","q":"How do you tokenize the targets and store the labels in the FLAN-T5 translation preprocessing?","a":"<p>Use the target tokenizer context and copy the ids into <code>labels</code>. <code>tokenizer.as_target_tokenizer()</code> is deprecated; use <code>text_target=</code> instead.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>with tokenizer.as_target_tokenizer():\n    labels = tokenizer(targets, max_length=128, truncation=True, padding=&quot;max_length&quot;)\nmodel_inputs[&quot;labels&quot;] = labels[&quot;input_ids&quot;]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0186","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-037-9-1-load-preprocess-convert","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s026","q":"How much training data does the preprocessing use?","a":"<p>The first 30000 training rows, mapped in batches. The test set is mapped in full.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>train_dataset = dataset[&#x27;train&#x27;].select(range(30000)).map(preprocess_data, batched=True)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0187","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-037-9-1-load-preprocess-convert","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s026","q":"How do you convert a Hugging Face dataset to <code>tf.data</code>, and why <code>collate_fn=None</code>?","a":"<p>Use <code>to_tf_dataset</code> with input columns and label columns. <code>collate_fn=None</code> avoids problems with incomplete batches.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>columns=[&#x27;input_ids&#x27;, &#x27;attention_mask&#x27;, &#x27;decoder_input_ids&#x27;],\nlabel_cols=[&#x27;labels&#x27;],\nshuffle=True,\nbatch_size=64,\ncollate_fn=None</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0188","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-037-9-1-load-preprocess-convert","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s026","q":"Which <code>shuffle</code> setting does the test dataset use in <code>to_tf_dataset</code>?","a":"<p><code>shuffle=False</code>, with <code>batch_size=64</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0189","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-038-9-2-freeze-the-pre-trained-layers","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s027","q":"How many parameters does FLAN-T5-base have, and how many are trainable after freezing?","a":"<p>About 247.6M total. After freezing, about <strong>222.9M are non-trainable and 24.7M trainable (~10%)</strong>. Only the output head learns.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0190","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-038-9-2-freeze-the-pre-trained-layers","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s027","q":"How do you freeze the pre-trained layers of FLAN-T5 in Keras?","a":"<p>Set <code>trainable = False</code> on the shared, encoder and decoder layers.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>model.get_layer(&quot;shared&quot;).trainable = False\nmodel.get_layer(&quot;encoder&quot;).trainable = False\nmodel.get_layer(&quot;decoder&quot;).trainable = False</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0191","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-038-9-2-freeze-the-pre-trained-layers","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s027","q":"How do you check the effect of freezing?","a":"<p>Call <code>model.summary()</code> before and after.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>model.summary()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0192","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-038-9-2-freeze-the-pre-trained-layers","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s027","q":"Why do you freeze the pre-trained layers?","a":"<p>To keep their knowledge and avoid overfitting.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0193","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-038-9-2-freeze-the-pre-trained-layers","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s027","q":"Why is <code>from_logits=True</code> mandatory for Hugging Face models?","a":"<p>They output raw logits (no softmax), so the loss must apply it internally.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0194","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-038-9-2-freeze-the-pre-trained-layers","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s027","q":"What are the exact parameter counts of FLAN-T5-base before and after freezing?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Count</th><th>Parameters</th><th>Size</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Total</td><td>247,577,856</td><td>944.43 MB</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Trainable</td><td>24,674,304</td><td>94.12 MB</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Non-trainable</td><td>222,903,552</td><td>850.31 MB</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0195","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-039-9-3-train-and-translate","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s028","q":"In Keras transfer learning on FLAN-T5, how do you compile and train the model with the default Adam optimizer and a train/validation split?","a":"<p>Compile with <code>adam</code> and <code>SparseCategoricalCrossentropy(from_logits=True)</code>, then call <code>fit</code> with the validation data for 3 epochs.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>model.compile(optimizer=&#x27;adam&#x27;,\n              loss=tf.keras.losses.SparseCategoricalCrossentropy(from_logits=True))\nmodel.fit(train_dataset, validation_data=test_dataset, epochs=3)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0196","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-039-9-3-train-and-translate","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s028","q":"What loss and validation-loss values show a healthy 3-epoch FLAN-T5 transfer-learning run, and how long does it take?","a":"<p>Loss falls about 25.6 → 1.45 → 0.78 and val_loss falls 2.52 → 0.84 → 0.62 over 3 epochs. The run takes about 11 minutes on a GPU.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0197","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-039-9-3-train-and-translate","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s028","q":"In a transfer-learning run, what does a rising validation loss with a falling training loss mean?","a":"<p>It means the model is overfitting.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0198","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-039-9-3-train-and-translate","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s028","q":"How do you write a <code>translate</code> function for a TF FLAN-T5 model that uses beam search with 4 beams and returns plain text?","a":"<p>Call <code>model.generate</code> on the batch's <code>input_ids</code> with <code>max_length=128</code>, <code>num_beams=4</code> and <code>early_stopping=True</code>, then decode with <code>skip_special_tokens=True</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def translate(inputs):\n    outputs = model.generate(inputs[0][&quot;input_ids&quot;], max_length=128, num_beams=4, early_stopping=True)\n    return tokenizer.decode(outputs[0], skip_special_tokens=True)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0199","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-039-9-3-train-and-translate","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s028","q":"How do you print the input, reference translation and model translation for 5 test batches?","a":"<p>Loop over <code>test_dataset.take(5)</code>, translate each batch, and decode the input ids and the label ids.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>for batch in test_dataset.take(5):\n    translated_text = translate(batch)\n    print(f&quot;Input: {tokenizer.decode(batch[0][&#x27;input_ids&#x27;][0], skip_special_tokens=True)}&quot;)\n    print(f&quot;Reference Translation: {tokenizer.decode(batch[1][0], skip_special_tokens=True)}&quot;)\n    print(f&quot;Translated Text: {translated_text}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0200","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-039-9-3-train-and-translate","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s028","q":"How does the Demo 2 transfer-learning notebook differ from Demo 1 when it adds quantitative evaluation?","a":"<p>It installs <code>rouge-score nltk</code>, tokenizes with <code>return_tensors=\"tf\"</code>, caps the test set at 2,000 rows (<code>shuffle=True</code>), and uses a small explicit learning rate via <code>tf_keras</code>. It trains without validation data.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0201","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-039-9-3-train-and-translate","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s028","q":"How do you compile and train in the Demo 2 transfer-learning notebook with an explicit learning rate of 2e-5?","a":"<p>Use the <code>tf_keras</code> Adam optimizer with <code>learning_rate=2e-5</code> and call <code>fit</code> on the train data only.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import tf_keras\nmodel.compile(optimizer=tf_keras.optimizers.Adam(learning_rate=2e-5),\n              loss=tf.keras.losses.SparseCategoricalCrossentropy(from_logits=True))\nmodel.fit(train_dataset, epochs=3)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0202","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-039-9-3-train-and-translate","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s028","q":"What three checks does the training-health function <code>evaluate_training_progress</code> compute from a Keras <code>history</code>?","a":"<p>It computes <code>loss_decreasing</code>, <code>val_loss_stable</code> and <code>no_overfitting</code>.</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><code>loss_decreasing</code>: the last loss is lower than the first loss.</li>\n  <li><code>val_loss_stable</code>: no validation loss exceeds 1.5 times the first validation loss.</li>\n  <li><code>no_overfitting</code>: the last validation loss is at most 1.1 times the minimum validation loss.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0203","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-039-9-3-train-and-translate","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s028","q":"In the transfer-learning efficiency calculation, how are <code>parameter_efficiency</code> and <code>memory_savings</code> defined?","a":"<p><code>parameter_efficiency</code> is trainable parameters divided by base parameters. <code>memory_savings</code> is (base − trainable) divided by base.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&#x27;parameter_efficiency&#x27;: trainable_params / base_params,\n&#x27;memory_savings&#x27;: (base_params - trainable_params) / base_params,</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0204","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-039-9-3-train-and-translate","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s028","q":"What is the approximate formula for <code>training_speedup</code> in the transfer-learning efficiency function?","a":"<p>It is 1 divided by the fraction of trainable parameters.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&#x27;training_speedup&#x27;: 1 / (trainable_params / base_params),  # Approximate</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0205","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-039-9-3-train-and-translate","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s028","q":"In FLAN-T5 transfer learning, what is the likely fix for each symptom: loss not decreasing, overfitting quickly, poor translation quality, memory errors, slow training?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Likely fix</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Loss not decreasing</td><td>Check learning rate; verify preprocessing</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Overfitting quickly</td><td>Lower learning rate; add regularisation</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Poor translation quality</td><td>Verify reference translations; check tokenisation</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Memory errors</td><td>Reduce batch size; gradient checkpointing</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Slow training</td><td>Confirm layers are really frozen; optimise the data pipeline</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0206","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-040-10-evaluation-metrics-rouge-bleu","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s029","q":"What question does ROUGE answer, and is it recall- or precision-oriented?","a":"<p>ROUGE asks how much of the reference content the output captured. It is recall-oriented, like checking the overlap of recipe ingredients.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0207","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-040-10-evaluation-metrics-rouge-bleu","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s029","q":"What question does BLEU answer, and is it recall- or precision-oriented?","a":"<p>BLEU asks how much of the output appears in the reference. It is precision-oriented (exact phrase match and order, 1–4-grams), like comparing finished dishes.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0208","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-040-10-evaluation-metrics-rouge-bleu","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s029","q":"What are the ROUGE variants?","a":"<p>ROUGE-1 (unigrams), ROUGE-2 (bigrams) and ROUGE-L (longest common subsequence).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0209","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-040-10-evaluation-metrics-rouge-bleu","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s029","q":"What are the BLEU variants and how are they combined?","a":"<p>BLEU-1 to BLEU-4. They are combined with a geometric mean and a brevity penalty.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0210","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-040-10-evaluation-metrics-rouge-bleu","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s029","q":"Which task is ROUGE typically used for, and which is BLEU typically used for?","a":"<p>ROUGE is typically used for summarisation. BLEU is typically used for translation. Use both, because they are complementary, and the metric should match the task.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0211","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-040-10-evaluation-metrics-rouge-bleu","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s029","q":"How do you compute ROUGE scores with <code>datasets</code> and print ROUGE-1, ROUGE-2 and ROUGE-L?","a":"<p>Load the metric with <code>load_metric(\"rouge\")</code>, call <code>compute</code> with predictions and references, and read the keys <code>rouge1</code>, <code>rouge2</code> and <code>rougeL</code>. Caveat: <code>load_metric</code> is deprecated and removed in newer <code>datasets</code>; use <code>evaluate</code> instead.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from datasets import load_metric\nrouge = load_metric(&quot;rouge&quot;)\nrouge_scores = rouge.compute(predictions=predictions, references=references)\nprint(f&quot;ROUGE-1: {rouge_scores[&#x27;rouge1&#x27;]}&quot;)  # Unigram overlap\nprint(f&quot;ROUGE-2: {rouge_scores[&#x27;rouge2&#x27;]}&quot;)  # Bigram overlap  \nprint(f&quot;ROUGE-L: {rouge_scores[&#x27;rougeL&#x27;]}&quot;)  # Longest common subsequence</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0212","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-040-10-evaluation-metrics-rouge-bleu","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s029","q":"How do you compute BLEU with <code>datasets</code>, and what does the <code>precisions</code> key hold?","a":"<p>Load <code>bleu</code> with <code>load_metric(\"bleu\")</code> and call <code>compute</code>. The <code>precisions</code> key holds the 1-gram to 4-gram precisions. Caveat: <code>load_metric</code> is deprecated and removed in newer <code>datasets</code>; use <code>evaluate</code> instead.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>bleu = load_metric(&quot;bleu&quot;)\nbleu_scores = bleu.compute(predictions=predictions, references=references)\nprint(f&quot;BLEU: {bleu_scores[&#x27;bleu&#x27;]}&quot;)\nprint(f&quot;Precisions: {bleu_scores[&#x27;precisions&#x27;]}&quot;)  # 1-gram to 4-gram</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0213","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-041-10-evaluation-metrics-rouge-bleu","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s029","q":"How does the hand-written <code>calculate_rouge_1_manual</code> compute ROUGE-1, and why is it recall-based?","a":"<p>It divides the number of overlapping words by the number of words in the reference, so it measures how much of the reference was captured.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>overlap = len(set(gen_words) &amp; set(ref_words))\nrouge_1 = overlap / len(ref_words)  # Recall-based</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0214","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-041-10-evaluation-metrics-rouge-bleu","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s029","q":"How does the hand-written <code>calculate_bleu_1_manual</code> compute BLEU-1, and why is it precision-based?","a":"<p>It divides the number of overlapping words by the number of words in the model output, so it measures how much of the output is in the reference.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>overlap = len(set(gen_words) &amp; set(ref_words))\nbleu_1 = overlap / len(gen_words)  # Precision-based</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0215","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-041-10-evaluation-metrics-rouge-bleu","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s029","q":"For the output \"The cat sat on the mat\" and the reference \"The cat is sitting on the mat\", what are the correct unigram recall and precision counting \"the\" twice?","a":"<p>5 words overlap. Unigram recall (ROUGE-1) is 5/7 ≈ 0.71 and precision (BLEU-1-style) is 5/6 ≈ 0.83. The output sentence has 6 words and the reference has 7.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0216","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-041-10-evaluation-metrics-rouge-bleu","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s029","q":"Why do the lecture's ROUGE-1 and BLEU-1 hand-calculation numbers (5/6 and 5/5) differ from what the code gives?","a":"<p>The code uses <code>set</code>, which counts \"the\" once, giving 4/7 and 4/6. The lecture quotes 5/6 and 5/5. The concept to remember is recall versus precision.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0217","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-042-10-1-the-notebook-scorer-rouge-score-nlt","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s030","q":"In the <code>rouge_score</code> scorer, what does <code>use_stemmer=True</code> do, and what does <code>SmoothingFunction().method4</code> do for BLEU?","a":"<p><code>use_stemmer=True</code> stems words before matching. <code>SmoothingFunction().method4</code> avoids a zero BLEU score on short sentences.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0218","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-042-10-1-the-notebook-scorer-rouge-score-nlt","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s030","q":"Which NLTK download does the FLAN-T5 BLEU scoring need before <code>nltk.word_tokenize</code> works?","a":"<p>The <code>punkt</code> tokenizer data.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>nltk.download(&#x27;punkt&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0219","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-042-10-1-the-notebook-scorer-rouge-score-nlt","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s030","q":"How do you build a ROUGE scorer for ROUGE-1, ROUGE-2 and ROUGE-L with stemming, and score a reference against a hypothesis?","a":"<p>Create a <code>RougeScorer</code> with the three metric names and <code>use_stemmer=True</code>, then call <code>score</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>rouge = rouge_scorer.RougeScorer([&#x27;rouge1&#x27;, &#x27;rouge2&#x27;, &#x27;rougeL&#x27;], use_stemmer=True)\nrouge_scores = rouge.score(reference, hypothesis)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0220","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-042-10-1-the-notebook-scorer-rouge-score-nlt","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s030","q":"How does the FLAN-T5 Chapter 3 Demo 2 evaluation compute a smoothed sentence-level BLEU score with <code>nltk</code>?","a":"<p>It tokenizes the reference and hypothesis with <code>nltk.word_tokenize</code>, wraps the reference tokens in a list, and calls <code>sentence_bleu</code> with the smoothing function.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>bleu_smoothing = SmoothingFunction().method4\nreference_tokens = [nltk.word_tokenize(reference)]\nhypothesis_tokens = nltk.word_tokenize(hypothesis)\nbleu_score = sentence_bleu(reference_tokens, hypothesis_tokens, smoothing_function=bleu_smoothing)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0221","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-042-10-1-the-notebook-scorer-rouge-score-nlt","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s030","q":"How does the FLAN-T5 Chapter 3 Demo 2 evaluation get the reference text for the first test batch before scoring?","a":"<p>It takes the first batch with <code>next(iter(test_dataset))</code> and decodes the label ids of the first row.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>batch = next(iter(test_dataset))\nreference_text = tokenizer.decode(batch[1][0], skip_special_tokens=True)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0222","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-042-10-1-the-notebook-scorer-rouge-score-nlt","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s030","q":"In the lecture's BLEU reading guide, what do the thresholds 0.4, 0.3, 0.2 and 0.1 mean?","a":"<p>0.4 or more is excellent, 0.3 or more is good, 0.2 or more is acceptable, 0.1 or more is poor but understandable, and below 0.1 is very poor.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0223","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-042-10-1-the-notebook-scorer-rouge-score-nlt","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s030","q":"What BLEU score did the WMT16 challenge reach, and how did the lecture rate it?","a":"<p>BLEU 0.12, which the lecture called acceptable for a new language pair.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0224","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-042-10-1-the-notebook-scorer-rouge-score-nlt","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s030","q":"Are the lecture's targets of ROUGE-1 &gt; 0.7 and BLEU &gt; 0.5 realistic?","a":"<p>No, they are optimistic. The BLEU actually seen was 0.1–0.2.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0225","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-043-11-challenge-wmt16-english-german-transf","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s031","q":"What is the setup of the <code>Chapter3_Solution</code> WMT16 challenge?","a":"<p>It uses the FLAN-T5 transfer-learning translation recipe (freeze <code>shared</code>, <code>encoder</code>, <code>decoder</code>) on WMT16 <code>de-en</code>, direction English→German, with FLAN-T5-base. It uses 30,000 train and 2,000 test rows, Adam 2e-5, 3 epochs, and BLEU evaluation on a batch.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0226","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-043-11-challenge-wmt16-english-german-transf","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s031","q":"How do you load the WMT16 English-German dataset with Hugging Face <code>datasets</code>?","a":"<p>Call <code>load_dataset</code> with <code>'wmt16'</code> and <code>'de-en'</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>dataset = load_dataset(&#x27;wmt16&#x27;, &#x27;de-en&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0227","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-043-11-challenge-wmt16-english-german-transf","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s031","q":"In the English→German preprocessing, what prompt prefix is used and where do inputs and targets come from?","a":"<p>The input is <code>Translate English to German:</code> followed by the English text, and the target is the German text, both from the <code>translation</code> field.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>inputs = [f&#x27;Translate English to German: {example[&quot;en&quot;]}&#x27; for example in examples[&#x27;translation&#x27;]]\ntargets = [example[&#x27;de&#x27;] for example in examples[&#x27;translation&#x27;]]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0228","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-043-11-challenge-wmt16-english-german-transf","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s031","q":"How do you tokenize inputs and labels for FLAN-T5 translation with a maximum length of 128?","a":"<p>Tokenize with <code>max_length=128</code>, <code>truncation=True</code> and <code>padding='max_length'</code>, then store the label ids under <code>labels</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>model_inputs = tokenizer(inputs, max_length=128, truncation=True, padding=&#x27;max_length&#x27;, return_tensors=&#x27;tf&#x27;)\nlabels = tokenizer(targets, max_length=128, truncation=True, padding=&#x27;max_length&#x27;, return_tensors=&#x27;tf&#x27;).input_ids\nmodel_inputs[&#x27;labels&#x27;] = labels</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0229","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-043-11-challenge-wmt16-english-german-transf","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s031","q":"How is <code>decoder_input_ids</code> filled in the WMT16 preprocessing?","a":"<p>The targets are tokenized again with the same settings, and their <code>input_ids</code> become <code>decoder_input_ids</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>decoder_inputs = tokenizer(targets, max_length=128, truncation=True, padding=&quot;max_length&quot;)\nmodel_inputs[&quot;decoder_input_ids&quot;] = decoder_inputs[&quot;input_ids&quot;]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0230","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-043-11-challenge-wmt16-english-german-transf","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s031","q":"How do you select 30,000 training rows and 2,000 test rows and map the preprocessing?","a":"<p>Use <code>select(range(...))</code> and <code>map(preprocess_data, batched=True)</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>train_dataset = dataset[&#x27;train&#x27;].select(range(30000)).map(preprocess_data, batched=True)\ntest_dataset = dataset[&#x27;test&#x27;].select(range(2000)).map(preprocess_data, batched=True)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0231","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-043-11-challenge-wmt16-english-german-transf","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s031","q":"How do you convert a tokenized Hugging Face dataset to a TF dataset for FLAN-T5 with <code>labels</code> as the label column?","a":"<p>Call <code>to_tf_dataset</code> with the model input columns, <code>label_cols=['labels']</code>, shuffle and batch size.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>train_dataset = train_dataset.to_tf_dataset(\n    columns=[&#x27;input_ids&#x27;, &#x27;attention_mask&#x27;, &#x27;decoder_input_ids&#x27;],\n    label_cols=[&#x27;labels&#x27;],\n    shuffle=True,\n    batch_size=64,\n    collate_fn=None\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0232","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-043-11-challenge-wmt16-english-german-transf","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s031","q":"In the WMT16 challenge, how is the model loaded and frozen, and what batch size is used?","a":"<p>The model load uses <code>google/flan-t5-base</code>, the same as the FLAN-T5 transfer-learning translation recipe. Freezing is the same three lines (<code>shared</code>, <code>encoder</code>, <code>decoder</code>), with <code>model.summary()</code> before and after. The batch size is 64.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0233","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-043-11-challenge-wmt16-english-german-transf","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s031","q":"How do you compile and train FLAN-T5 in the WMT16 challenge?","a":"<p>Compile with Adam at learning rate 2e-5 and <code>SparseCategoricalCrossentropy(from_logits=True)</code>, then fit for 3 epochs with validation data.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>model.compile(optimizer=tf.keras.optimizers.Adam(learning_rate=2e-5),\n              loss=tf.keras.losses.SparseCategoricalCrossentropy(from_logits=True))\nmodel.fit(train_dataset, validation_data=test_dataset, epochs=3)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0234","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-044-11-challenge-wmt16-english-german-transf","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s031","q":"How does the batch BLEU evaluation score a whole batch of translations?","a":"<p>It generates for a whole batch, decodes each reference and hypothesis, scores each pair with <code>calculate_bleu</code>, and averages the scores.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>outputs = model.generate(inputs, max_length=128, num_beams=4, early_stopping=True)\nfor i in range(len(inputs)):\n    reference = tokenizer.decode(references[i], skip_special_tokens=True)\n    hypothesis = tokenizer.decode(outputs[i], skip_special_tokens=True)\n    bleu_score = calculate_bleu(reference, hypothesis)\n    bleu_scores.append(bleu_score)\nreturn sum(bleu_scores) / len(bleu_scores)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0235","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-044-11-challenge-wmt16-english-german-transf","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s031","q":"Which batch does <code>translate_and_evaluate</code> score, and where do its inputs and references come from?","a":"<p>It scores the first batch of the dataset, taken with <code>next(iter(dataset))</code>. Inputs are <code>batch[0]['input_ids']</code> and references are <code>batch[1]</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>batch = next(iter(dataset))\ninputs = batch[0][&#x27;input_ids&#x27;]\nreferences = batch[1]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0236","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-044-11-challenge-wmt16-english-german-transf","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s031","q":"What results did the WMT16 English→German challenge give?","a":"<p>BLEU ≈ 0.12, which is acceptable for a hard language pair after a short head-only run. Training took about 10–15 min on a GPU, with about 10% of parameters trained.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0237","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-044-11-challenge-wmt16-english-german-transf","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s031","q":"What prompt does the lecture's German→English variant use?","a":"<p><code>\"translate German to English: {german}\"</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0238","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-045-12-1-peft-in-one-view","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s032","q":"What is Parameter-Efficient Fine-Tuning (PEFT)?","a":"<p>PEFT modifies a small subset of parameters (or adds small modules) instead of retraining the whole model. It gets strong task performance with limited data and compute.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0239","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-045-12-1-peft-in-one-view","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s032","q":"What is the recipe analogy for full fine-tuning, transfer learning and PEFT?","a":"<p>Full fine-tuning is reworking the recipe. Transfer learning is adding a sauce (a new head). PEFT is specialised tools (adapters) that enhance the dish without altering the recipe.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0240","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-045-12-1-peft-in-one-view","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s032","q":"Compare traditional fine-tuning, transfer learning and PEFT on parameters updated, data needed, compute and storage per task.","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th></th><th>Traditional fine-tuning</th><th>Transfer learning</th><th>PEFT</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Parameters updated</td><td>All</td><td>New layers + some base layers</td><td>Small adapter modules only</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Data needed</td><td>Large</td><td>Medium</td><td>Small</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Compute / training time</td><td>High / long</td><td>Medium / medium</td><td>Low / fast</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Storage per task</td><td>Full model copy</td><td>Modified model per task</td><td>Base model + small adapters</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0241","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-045-12-1-peft-in-one-view","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s032","q":"What are the advantages of PEFT?","a":"<p>It works with limited data, costs less, trains faster, and lets one shared base model serve many tasks with swappable per-task adapters.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0242","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-045-12-1-peft-in-one-view","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s032","q":"What are the lecture's rules of thumb for PEFT's savings?","a":"<p>About 0.1–1% of parameters trained, about 10x faster, about 5x less memory, and 95–99% of full fine-tuning quality.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0243","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-045-12-1-peft-in-one-view","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s032","q":"When should you use PEFT?","a":"<p>Use PEFT when compute or data is limited, when you serve many tasks from one model, or when you are prototyping.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0244","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-046-12-2-adapters-the-idea-lora-refines","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s033","q":"What is an adapter in a transformer layer?","a":"<p>An adapter is a bottleneck module inserted into a transformer layer. It does down-project → non-linearity → up-project, and the result is added back through a residual connection.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0245","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-046-12-2-adapters-the-idea-lora-refines","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s033","q":"How is a bottleneck <code>Adapter</code> implemented in PyTorch?","a":"<p>It has a <code>down_project</code> linear layer to <code>adapter_dim</code>, a ReLU, and an <code>up_project</code> linear layer back to <code>input_dim</code>. The forward pass adds the result to the input.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>class Adapter(nn.Module):\n    def __init__(self, input_dim, adapter_dim=64):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.down_project = nn.Linear(input_dim, adapter_dim)\n        self.activation = nn.ReLU()\n        self.up_project = nn.Linear(adapter_dim, input_dim)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0246","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-046-12-2-adapters-the-idea-lora-refines","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s033","q":"What does the forward pass of the PyTorch <code>Adapter</code> return?","a":"<p>It returns the input plus the adapter output (a residual connection).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>return x + self.up_project(self.activation(self.down_project(x)))</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0247","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-046-12-2-adapters-the-idea-lora-refines","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s033","q":"What is the default bottleneck size <code>adapter_dim</code> of the <code>Adapter</code> class, and how does <code>add_adapter_to_layer</code> attach it?","a":"<p>The default <code>adapter_dim</code> is 64. The function sets <code>layer.adapter</code> to a new <code>Adapter</code> built from <code>layer.hidden_size</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>layer.adapter = Adapter(layer.hidden_size, adapter_dim)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0248","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-047-12-3-lora-low-rank-adaptation-the-math","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s034","q":"What does LoRA do to the original weight matrix W, and what does it learn instead?","a":"<p>LoRA keeps W frozen (for example 512×512 = 262,144 parameters). It learns a low-rank update ΔW = A × B, where A is (in × r), B is (r × out) and r (the rank) is tiny.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0249","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-047-12-3-lora-low-rank-adaptation-the-math","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s034","q":"What is the LoRA output formula?","a":"<p>Output = <code>W·x + (x·A·B)</code>. In the PyTorch version it is scaled by <code>alpha / r</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0250","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-047-12-3-lora-low-rank-adaptation-the-math","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s034","q":"How many trainable parameters does LoRA with r = 1 need for a 512×512 matrix, and what is the reduction?","a":"<p>512×1×2 = 1,024 trainable parameters, about a 256x reduction.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0251","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-047-12-3-lora-low-rank-adaptation-the-math","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s034","q":"Why is B initialised to zeros in the PyTorch LoRA version?","a":"<p>So training starts exactly at the pre-trained behaviour.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0252","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-047-12-3-lora-low-rank-adaptation-the-math","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s034","q":"How does the PyTorch <code>LoRALayer</code> create its A and B matrices and freeze the original layer?","a":"<p>A is random normal scaled by 0.01 with shape (rank, in_dim), B is zeros with shape (out_dim, rank), and the original layer's parameters get <code>requires_grad = False</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>self.lora_A = nn.Parameter(torch.randn(rank, in_dim) * 0.01)\nself.lora_B = nn.Parameter(torch.zeros(out_dim, rank))\nfor param in self.original_layer.parameters():\n    param.requires_grad = False</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0253","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-047-12-3-lora-low-rank-adaptation-the-math","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s034","q":"What are the default <code>rank</code> and <code>alpha</code> of the PyTorch <code>LoRALayer</code>, and how is the LoRA output scaled?","a":"<p>The defaults are <code>rank=4</code> and <code>alpha=16</code>. The LoRA output is multiplied by <code>alpha / rank</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def __init__(self, original_layer, rank=4, alpha=16):\nlora_output = (x @ self.lora_A.T @ self.lora_B.T) * (self.alpha / self.rank)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0254","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-047-12-3-lora-low-rank-adaptation-the-math","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s034","q":"What does the forward pass of the PyTorch <code>LoRALayer</code> return?","a":"<p>It returns the original layer's output plus the scaled LoRA output.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>return original_output + lora_output</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0255","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-047-12-3-lora-low-rank-adaptation-the-math","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s034","q":"How does <code>calculate_lora_efficiency</code> compute the LoRA parameter count and the reduction factor for a square matrix?","a":"<p>Original parameters are <code>matrix_size * matrix_size</code>. LoRA parameters are <code>2 * matrix_size * rank</code> (A and B). The reduction factor is original divided by LoRA parameters.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>original_params = matrix_size * matrix_size\nlora_params = 2 * matrix_size * rank  # A and B matrices\nreduction_factor = original_params / lora_params</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0256","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-048-12-4-lora-with-the-hugging-face-peft-lib","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s035","q":"What does <code>target_modules</code> do in a LoRA config, and what values are used for T5 and for Llama-style models?","a":"<p><code>target_modules</code> picks which layers get adapters. For T5 it is the attention <code>q</code> and <code>v</code>. For Llama-style models it is <code>q_proj</code>, <code>v_proj</code>, <code>k_proj</code>, <code>o_proj</code>, plus optionally <code>gate_proj</code>/<code>up_proj</code>/<code>down_proj</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0257","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-048-12-4-lora-with-the-hugging-face-peft-lib","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s035","q":"How do you configure LoRA for a seq2seq model with <code>peft</code>, with rank 8, alpha 32 and dropout 0.1?","a":"<p>Build a <code>LoraConfig</code> with <code>TaskType.SEQ_2_SEQ_LM</code>, <code>r=8</code>, <code>lora_alpha=32</code>, <code>lora_dropout=0.1</code> and <code>target_modules=[\"q\", \"v\"]</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>lora_config = LoraConfig(\n    task_type=TaskType.SEQ_2_SEQ_LM,\n    inference_mode=False,\n    r=8,  # Rank\n    lora_alpha=32,  # Scaling parameter\n    lora_dropout=0.1,\n    target_modules=[&quot;q&quot;, &quot;v&quot;]  # Target attention layers\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0258","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-048-12-4-lora-with-the-hugging-face-peft-lib","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s035","q":"How do you apply a LoRA config to a base model with <code>peft</code> and print the trainable parameters?","a":"<p>Call <code>get_peft_model</code> with the base model and the config, then call <code>print_trainable_parameters</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>peft_model = get_peft_model(base_model, lora_config)\npeft_model.print_trainable_parameters()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0259","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-048-12-4-lora-with-the-hugging-face-peft-lib","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s035","q":"What is the intro-lecture variant of the <code>peft</code> LoRA config, and what output does it give?","a":"<p>It uses <code>r=16, lora_alpha=32, target_modules=[\"q\",\"v\"], lora_dropout=0.1, bias=\"none\", task_type=\"SEQ_2_SEQ_LM\"</code>. The example output is <code>trainable params: 294,912 || all params: 247,872,768 || trainable%: 0.12</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0260","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-048-12-4-lora-with-the-hugging-face-peft-lib","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s035","q":"Why does a PyTorch loop over all of <code>model.parameters()</code> effectively train only the LoRA parameters of a PEFT model?","a":"<p>Only the LoRA params have <code>requires_grad</code>, so the optimiser effectively updates just those.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0261","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-048-12-4-lora-with-the-hugging-face-peft-lib","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s035","q":"What does the PEFT training loop do in each step?","a":"<p>It zeroes the gradients, runs the model on the batch, takes <code>outputs.loss</code>, backpropagates, steps the optimiser and adds up the loss. The optimiser is <code>AdamW</code> with <code>lr=1e-4</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>optimizer = torch.optim.AdamW(model.parameters(), lr=1e-4)\noptimizer.zero_grad()\noutputs = model(**batch)\nloss = outputs.loss\nloss.backward()\noptimizer.step()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0262","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-049-12-4-lora-with-the-hugging-face-peft-lib","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s035","q":"How does <code>peft_inference</code> format the prompt for translation and for summarisation?","a":"<p>For translation it uses <code>translate English to Spanish:</code> followed by the text. For summarisation it uses <code>summarize:</code> followed by the text. Other tasks use the raw input.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>formatted_input = f&quot;translate English to Spanish: {input_text}&quot;\nformatted_input = f&quot;summarize: {input_text}&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0263","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-049-12-4-lora-with-the-hugging-face-peft-lib","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s035","q":"How does <code>peft_inference</code> tokenize the input and run generation?","a":"<p>It tokenizes with <code>return_tensors=\"pt\"</code>, <code>max_length=512</code> and truncation, then generates under <code>torch.no_grad()</code> with <code>max_length=150</code>, <code>num_beams=4</code> and early stopping.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>inputs = tokenizer(formatted_input, return_tensors=&quot;pt&quot;, max_length=512, \nwith torch.no_grad():\n    outputs = model.generate(**inputs, max_length=150, num_beams=4, </code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0264","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-050-12-5-one-base-model-many-task-adapters","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s036","q":"What is the idea of the <code>MultiTaskPEFT</code> class?","a":"<p>It holds one base model and a dictionary <code>task_adapters</code> of per-task LoRA adapters. You add an adapter for each task with <code>add_task_adapter</code> and pick one with <code>switch_task</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0265","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-050-12-5-one-base-model-many-task-adapters","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s036","q":"How does <code>MultiTaskPEFT.add_task_adapter</code> create and store an adapter?","a":"<p>It calls <code>get_peft_model</code> on the base model with the LoRA config and stores the result under the task name.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>adapter_model = get_peft_model(self.base_model, lora_config)\nself.task_adapters[task_name] = adapter_model</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0266","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-050-12-5-one-base-model-many-task-adapters","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s036","q":"What does <code>switch_task</code> do when the task name is unknown?","a":"<p>It raises a <code>ValueError</code> saying the task was not found.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>raise ValueError(f&quot;Task {task_name} not found&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0267","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-050-12-5-one-base-model-many-task-adapters","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s036","q":"What does <code>get_storage_efficiency</code> of <code>MultiTaskPEFT</code> compare?","a":"<p>It compares the trainable adapter parameters with the base model parameters multiplied by the number of tasks, to show the storage savings against full fine-tuning.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&#x27;storage_efficiency&#x27;: adapter_size / (base_size * len(self.task_adapters))</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0268","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-050-12-5-one-base-model-many-task-adapters","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s036","q":"What is the caveat of calling <code>get_peft_model</code> repeatedly on the same <code>base_model</code>?","a":"<p>It injects adapters into the base model in place. In real code, load the base model once and use the <code>peft</code> multi-adapter API (<code>add_adapter</code> / <code>set_adapter</code> / <code>load_adapter</code>), or reload the base per adapter.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0269","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-051-12-5-one-base-model-many-task-adapters","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s036","q":"How do you measure the parameter efficiency of a PEFT model against its base model?","a":"<p>Count the base parameters and the trainable parameters (<code>requires_grad</code>). The efficiency ratio is trainable divided by base, and the reduction factor is base divided by trainable.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>base_params = sum(p.numel() for p in base_model.parameters())\ntrainable_params = sum(p.numel() for p in peft_model.parameters() if p.requires_grad)\n&#x27;efficiency_ratio&#x27;: trainable_params / base_params,\n&#x27;reduction_factor&#x27;: base_params / trainable_params</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0270","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-051-12-5-one-base-model-many-task-adapters","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s036","q":"What is the idea of the <code>AdaptiveLoRA</code> dynamic-rank class?","a":"<p>It allocates <code>max_rank</code> rows but uses only the first <code>current_rank</code> of them, plus learnable per-rank weights, so the rank can be adapted during training.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0271","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-051-12-5-one-base-model-many-task-adapters","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s036","q":"How does <code>AdaptiveLoRA</code> adjust its effective rank?","a":"<p><code>adapt_rank</code> sets <code>current_rank</code> to the smaller of the new rank and <code>max_rank</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>self.current_rank = min(new_rank, self.max_rank)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0272","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-051-12-5-one-base-model-many-task-adapters","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s036","q":"How does <code>AdaptiveLoRA</code> slice its matrices in the forward pass?","a":"<p>It keeps only the first <code>current_rank</code> rows of <code>lora_A</code>, the first <code>current_rank</code> columns of <code>lora_B</code>, and the first <code>current_rank</code> rank weights.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>A_active = self.lora_A[:self.current_rank, :]\nB_active = self.lora_B[:, :self.current_rank]\nweights_active = self.rank_weights[:self.current_rank]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0273","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-052-12-6-lora-peft-guidelines-lecture-as-a-t","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s037","q":"What are the lecture's guidelines for the LoRA rank <code>r</code> by task size?","a":"<p>Small tasks use 1–4 (most efficient), medium tasks use 8–16 (balanced), and complex tasks use 32–64 (more capacity).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0274","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-052-12-6-lora-peft-guidelines-lecture-as-a-t","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s037","q":"What is the common heuristic for <code>lora_alpha</code>, and what range is used for <code>lora_dropout</code>?","a":"<p><code>lora_alpha</code> is commonly <code>2 × rank</code>. <code>lora_dropout</code> is 0.05–0.1 for regularisation.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0275","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-052-12-6-lora-peft-guidelines-lecture-as-a-t","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s037","q":"What learning rate range does the lecture suggest for LoRA, and how does it compare with full fine-tuning?","a":"<p>1e-4 to 1e-3, which is higher than full fine-tuning.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0276","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-052-12-6-lora-peft-guidelines-lecture-as-a-t","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s037","q":"Which target modules does the lecture suggest for LoRA first, and which for more capacity?","a":"<p>Attention projections first. Feed-forward layers and embeddings/<code>lm_head</code> for more capacity.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0277","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-052-12-6-lora-peft-guidelines-lecture-as-a-t","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s037","q":"How much data does LoRA/PEFT fine-tuning need according to the lecture guidelines?","a":"<p>About 100–1,000 examples minimum, and 1,000–10,000 is good. Quality beats quantity.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0278","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-052-12-6-lora-peft-guidelines-lecture-as-a-t","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s037","q":"What batch size and number of epochs does the lecture suggest to start LoRA/PEFT training?","a":"<p>Start with a batch size of 16–32 (memory-bound) and 3–10 epochs, which is usually enough.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0279","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-052-12-6-lora-peft-guidelines-lecture-as-a-t","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s037","q":"How do you measure the average inference time of a model over a list of prompts?","a":"<p>Record <code>time.time()</code> before and after tokenizing, generating and decoding each prompt, add up the elapsed times and divide by the number of prompts. This measures latency, which is distinct from accuracy.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>start_time = time.time()\nend_time = time.time()\ntotal_time += (end_time - start_time)\navg_time = total_time / len(test_prompts)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0280","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-053-13-1-overfitting-vs-generalisability","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s038","q":"What is the difference between an overfit and a generalisable model?","a":"<p>An overfit model is tuned to a few palates. A generalisable model suits many.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0281","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-053-13-1-overfitting-vs-generalisability","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s038","q":"What is the sign of overfitting during LoRA training, and what are the remedies?","a":"<p>Validation loss stalls or rises while training loss keeps falling. Remedies are lower rank, early stopping, regularisation and more data.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0282","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-053-13-1-overfitting-vs-generalisability","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s038","q":"How does <code>monitor_overfitting</code> decide that overfitting happened?","a":"<p>It looks at the last <code>patience</code> validation losses. If all of them are at least as large as the best earlier validation loss, it reports overfitting.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>overfitting_detected = all(val_loss &gt;= best_val for val_loss in recent_val)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0283","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-053-13-1-overfitting-vs-generalisability","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s038","q":"What does <code>monitor_overfitting</code> recommend and what is the default patience?","a":"<p>The default <code>patience</code> is 3. It recommends <code>reduce_rank</code> if overfitting is detected and <code>continue</code> otherwise.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&#x27;recommendation&#x27;: &#x27;reduce_rank&#x27; if overfitting_detected else &#x27;continue&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0284","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-053-13-1-overfitting-vs-generalisability","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s038","q":"What does <code>monitor_overfitting</code> return when there are too few validation losses, and what is <code>train_val_gap</code>?","a":"<p>It returns <code>False</code> when there are fewer than <code>patience + 1</code> validation losses. Otherwise the result includes <code>train_val_gap</code>, the last training loss minus the last validation loss.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>if len(val_losses) &lt; patience + 1:\n    return False\n&#x27;train_val_gap&#x27;: train_losses[-1] - val_losses[-1],</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0285","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-054-13-2-choosing-the-rank","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s039","q":"Is a higher LoRA rank always better, and where should you start?","a":"<p>No. Higher rank means more capacity and parameters and a higher risk of overfitting. Start low (1–4) and increase while validation improves.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0286","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-054-13-2-choosing-the-rank","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s039","q":"How does <code>analyze_rank_impact</code> compute the parameters and memory of a LoRA rank?","a":"<p>Parameters are <code>2 * base_dim * rank</code> (A and B matrices). Memory in MB is parameters times 4 (float32) divided by 1e6.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>params = 2 * base_dim * rank  # A and B matrices\n&#x27;memory_mb&#x27;: params * 4 / 1e6,  # Float32</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0287","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-054-13-2-choosing-the-rank","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s039","q":"In <code>get_rank_recommendation</code>, how is the ratio rank / base_dim interpreted?","a":"<p>Under 0.01 is very efficient but may underfit. Under 0.05 is a good balance for most tasks. Under 0.1 is higher capacity, so watch for overfitting. Above that is high capacity and likely to overfit.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0288","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-054-13-2-choosing-the-rank","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s039","q":"What are the default ranks tried by <code>analyze_rank_impact</code>?","a":"<p>The ranks are 1, 2, 4, 8, 16 and 32.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def analyze_rank_impact(base_dim, ranks=[1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32]):</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0289","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-055-13-2-choosing-the-rank","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s039","q":"How does the progressive rank search choose the optimal LoRA rank?","a":"<p>It starts at <code>start_rank</code> and doubles the rank each round up to <code>max_rank</code>. It trains and scores each rank, keeps the best, and stops when the score drops below 95% of the best.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>elif score &lt; best_score * 0.95:  # Performance degraded\n    break\ncurrent_rank *= 2</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0290","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-055-13-2-choosing-the-rank","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s039","q":"What <code>LoraConfig</code> does the progressive rank search build for each rank?","a":"<p><code>r</code> equals the current rank and <code>lora_alpha</code> equals twice the current rank.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>lora_config = LoraConfig(r=current_rank, lora_alpha=current_rank*2)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0291","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-055-13-2-choosing-the-rank","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s039","q":"How does <code>AdaptiveLoRAConfig.adapt_rank</code> raise or lower the rank?","a":"<p>It needs at least 3 recorded performances. If all of the last 3 are below the target (default 0.9), it doubles the rank up to 64. If all are above 1.1 times the target, it halves the rank down to 1. Otherwise it keeps the base rank.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>new_rank = min(self.base_rank * 2, 64)\nnew_rank = max(self.base_rank // 2, 1)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0292","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-055-13-2-choosing-the-rank","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s039","q":"What LoRA config does <code>AdaptiveLoRAConfig.get_lora_config</code> return?","a":"<p>It uses the chosen rank with <code>lora_alpha=rank * 2</code> (a common heuristic), <code>lora_dropout=0.1</code> and <code>target_modules=[\"q_proj\", \"v_proj\"]</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>return LoraConfig(\n    r=rank,\n    lora_alpha=rank * 2,  # Common heuristic\n    lora_dropout=0.1,\n    target_modules=[&quot;q_proj&quot;, &quot;v_proj&quot;]\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0293","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-056-13-3-learning-rate-batch-size-epochs","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s040","q":"What is a learning-rate range test for LoRA and how does the lecture pick the final rate?","a":"<p>Try an exponential sweep of learning rates for a few batches each. The lecture picks the learning rate with the steepest descent in loss and divides it by 10 to be conservative.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>optimal_idx = np.argmin(np.gradient(losses))\n&#x27;recommendation&#x27;: optimal_lr / 10  # Conservative choice</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0294","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-056-13-3-learning-rate-batch-size-epochs","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s040","q":"What range does <code>find_optimal_learning_rate</code> sweep, and how many rates and batches does it test?","a":"<p>It sweeps from 1e-5 to 1e-2 with 20 log-spaced rates (<code>np.logspace</code>), and tests only the first 10 batches for each.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def find_optimal_learning_rate(model, train_data, lr_range=(1e-5, 1e-2)):\nlrs = np.logspace(np.log10(lr_range[0]), np.log10(lr_range[1]), 20)\nif i &gt;= 10:  # Test only few batches</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0295","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-057-13-4-cross-validation-regularisation-mon","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s041","q":"How does <code>cross_validate_lora</code> choose a LoRA rank?","a":"<p>It runs k-fold cross-validation (default 5 folds) over the candidate ranks (default 4, 8, 16). It trains and scores each fold, averages the scores per rank, and returns the rank with the best mean score.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>kfold = KFold(n_splits=k_folds, shuffle=True, random_state=42)\nbest_rank = max(results.keys(), key=lambda r: results[r][&#x27;mean_score&#x27;])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0296","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-057-13-4-cross-validation-regularisation-mon","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s041","q":"What does <code>cross_validate_lora</code> record for each rank?","a":"<p>It records the mean score, the standard deviation and the list of fold scores.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&#x27;mean_score&#x27;: np.mean(fold_scores),\n&#x27;std_score&#x27;: np.std(fold_scores),\n&#x27;fold_scores&#x27;: fold_scores</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0297","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-057-13-4-cross-validation-regularisation-mon","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s041","q":"Which parameters does <code>apply_lora_regularization</code> penalise, and with which penalties?","a":"<p>Only the LoRA matrices, whose names contain <code>lora_A</code> or <code>lora_B</code>. It applies an L1 penalty (default 0.01) and an L2 penalty (default 0.001).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>if &#x27;lora_A&#x27; in name or &#x27;lora_B&#x27; in name:\n    l1_loss += torch.sum(torch.abs(param))\n    l2_loss += torch.sum(param ** 2)\nreturn l1_lambda * l1_loss + l2_lambda * l2_loss</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0298","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-057-13-4-cross-validation-regularisation-mon","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s041","q":"How is the regularisation penalty used in the training loop?","a":"<p>It is added to the base loss before backpropagation.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>total_loss = base_loss + reg_loss\ntotal_loss.backward()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0299","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-058-13-4-cross-validation-regularisation-mon","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s041","q":"What does <code>LoRATrainingMonitor</code> do, and what are its defaults?","a":"<p>It is an early-stopping monitor with patience on the validation score and an overfitting-gap check. The defaults are <code>patience=5</code> and <code>min_delta=0.001</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def __init__(self, patience=5, min_delta=0.001):</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0300","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-058-13-4-cross-validation-regularisation-mon","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s041","q":"When does <code>LoRATrainingMonitor</code> count an epoch as improved or trigger early stopping?","a":"<p>A validation score above the best score plus <code>min_delta</code> resets the wait counter and returns <code>continue</code>. Otherwise the wait counter grows, and once it reaches <code>patience</code> the monitor returns the <code>stop</code> action.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>if val_score &gt; self.best_score + self.min_delta:\nif self.wait &gt;= self.patience:\n    return {&#x27;action&#x27;: &#x27;stop&#x27;, &#x27;message&#x27;: &#x27;Early stopping triggered&#x27;}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0301","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-058-13-4-cross-validation-regularisation-mon","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s041","q":"How does <code>LoRATrainingMonitor</code> detect overfitting and what does it recommend?","a":"<p>The overfitting gap is train loss minus validation loss. If the last 3 gaps are all below −0.1 (validation loss much higher than train loss), it returns the <code>reduce_rank</code> action.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>if all(gap &lt; -0.1 for gap in recent_gaps):  # Val loss much higher than train\n    return {&#x27;action&#x27;: &#x27;reduce_rank&#x27;, &#x27;message&#x27;: &#x27;Overfitting detected&#x27;}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0302","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-058-13-4-cross-validation-regularisation-mon","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s041","q":"What recommendations does <code>get_recommendations</code> give from the last 3 epochs?","a":"<p>If validation scores keep improving, it says to continue training. If validation losses keep increasing, it says to consider reducing the learning rate. Otherwise it says performance plateaued, so consider adjusting hyperparameters.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0303","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-058-13-4-cross-validation-regularisation-mon","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s041","q":"What are the common pitfalls when tuning LoRA?","a":"<p>Rank too high (overfits, wasteful), learning rate too high (unstable), too little monitoring, no regularisation, and stopping before convergence.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0304","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-059-14-lora-in-tensorflow-implementation-exp","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s042","q":"What is the goal of the Chapter 4 LoRA notebooks in TensorFlow?","a":"<p>Freeze the pre-trained FLAN-T5, wrap a dense layer with trainable low-rank matrices A and B, and fine-tune for English→German (WMT16).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0305","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-059-14-lora-in-tensorflow-implementation-exp","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s042","q":"Which notebooks make up the Chapter 4 LoRA material?","a":"<p><code>Chapter4_Demo1_LoRA_FineTuning_FLAN_T5</code>, <code>Chapter4_Demo2_LoRA_Experiments</code> and <code>Chapter4_Solution</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0306","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-060-14-1-data-prep-wmt16-de-en-20-000-train","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s043","q":"Which install command do the Chapter 4 LoRA TensorFlow notebooks use?","a":"<p>They install transformers, tensorflow, datasets and tensorflow_addons.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>!pip install transformers tensorflow datasets tensorflow_addons</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0307","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-060-14-1-data-prep-wmt16-de-en-20-000-train","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s043","q":"How does the LoRA data prep differ from the WMT16 challenge data prep?","a":"<p>It uses the same preprocessing with a smaller subset and a larger batch: 20,000 train rows, 1,000 test rows and batch size 128.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0308","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-060-14-1-data-prep-wmt16-de-en-20-000-train","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s043","q":"What copy-paste slips are in Demo 1's data prep, and which dataset should you use?","a":"<p>Demo 1 mistakenly loads <code>abisee/cnn_dailymail</code> while its preprocessing expects a <code>translation</code> field, and its markdown intro says \"sentiment analysis\". Use WMT16 as in Demo 2 and the Solution.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0309","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-060-14-1-data-prep-wmt16-de-en-20-000-train","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s043","q":"How do you load the FLAN-T5-base tokenizer in the LoRA TensorFlow notebooks?","a":"<p>Use <code>AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained</code> with <code>'google/flan-t5-base'</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(&#x27;google/flan-t5-base&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0310","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-060-14-1-data-prep-wmt16-de-en-20-000-train","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s043","q":"How do you select the 20,000 train and 1,000 test rows in the LoRA data prep?","a":"<p>Use <code>select(range(...))</code> and then <code>map</code> the preprocessing.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>train_dataset = dataset[&#x27;train&#x27;].select(range(20000)).map(preprocess_data, batched=True)\ntest_dataset = dataset[&#x27;test&#x27;].select(range(1000)).map(preprocess_data, batched=True)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0311","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-060-14-1-data-prep-wmt16-de-en-20-000-train","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s043","q":"In the LoRA data prep, which TF dataset settings differ between train and test?","a":"<p>Both use batch size 128. The train set uses <code>shuffle=True</code> and the test set uses <code>shuffle=False</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>batch_size=128,\nshuffle=False,</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0312","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-061-14-2-the-keras-loralayer","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s044","q":"What does the Keras <code>LoRALayer</code> compute?","a":"<p><code>output = dense(x) + (x @ A) @ B</code>. A is (input_dim × rank) and B is (rank × units). Both are trainable and the wrapped dense layer is frozen. <code>rank</code> is the bottleneck width (default 4).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0313","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-061-14-2-the-keras-loralayer","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s044","q":"How does the Keras <code>LoRALayer</code> create its A and B weights?","a":"<p>In <code>build</code> it adds two trainable weights with <code>random_normal</code> initialisation: <code>w_a</code> of shape (input dim, rank) and <code>w_b</code> of shape (rank, dense units).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>self.w_a = self.add_weight(shape=(input_shape[-1], self.rank),\nself.w_b = self.add_weight(shape=(self.rank, self.dense.units),</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0314","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-061-14-2-the-keras-loralayer","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s044","q":"What does the <code>call</code> method of the Keras <code>LoRALayer</code> do?","a":"<p>It computes the original dense output and the LoRA output (<code>inputs @ w_a @ w_b</code>), sets the dense layer to non-trainable, and returns the sum.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>original_output = self.dense(inputs)\nlora_output = tf.matmul(tf.matmul(inputs, self.w_a), self.w_b)\nself.dense.trainable = False\nreturn original_output + lora_output</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0315","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-061-14-2-the-keras-loralayer","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s044","q":"How does the Keras <code>LoRALayer</code> differ from the PyTorch LoRA version?","a":"<p>Both matrices use <code>random_normal</code> in Keras, with no zero-init for B, and there is no <code>alpha/rank</code> scaling.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0316","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-061-14-2-the-keras-loralayer","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s044","q":"What do the lecture sketches <code>explore_model_layers</code>, <code>apply_lora_to_model</code> and <code>recursive_lora_replacement</code> admit about replacing layers?","a":"<p>Their own comments say real layer replacement \"requires more complex model reconstruction\". The notebook approach is the working version.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0317","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-061-14-2-the-keras-loralayer","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s044","q":"How do you load FLAN-T5-base as a TF seq2seq model for LoRA?","a":"<p>Use <code>TFAutoModelForSeq2SeqLM.from_pretrained</code> with <code>'google/flan-t5-base'</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>model = TFAutoModelForSeq2SeqLM.from_pretrained(&#x27;google/flan-t5-base&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0318","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-062-14-2-the-keras-loralayer","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s044","q":"How do you inspect the structure of a FLAN-T5 TF model before choosing layers for LoRA?","a":"<p>Call <code>model.summary()</code> and list the decoder's layers with <code>_flatten_layers()</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>model.summary()\n[layer for layer in model.decoder._flatten_layers()]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0319","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-062-14-2-the-keras-loralayer","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s044","q":"How does <code>explore_model_layers</code> find the dense layers for LoRA replacement?","a":"<p>It flattens the decoder layers and prints each layer's type name. For layers whose type contains <code>Dense</code> it prints the number of units.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>flattened_layers = list(model.decoder._flatten_layers())\nif &#x27;Dense&#x27; in layer_type:\n    print(f&quot;  -&gt; Dense layer found: {layer.units} units&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0320","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-062-14-2-the-keras-loralayer","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s044","q":"What does Demo 1's freeze-and-wrap loop do, and what is <code>model.layers[3]</code>?","a":"<p>The loop freezes the decoder layers, and <code>model.layers[3]</code> is the <code>lm_head</code>, which is wrapped in a <code>LoRALayer</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>model.get_layer(&#x27;encoder&#x27;).trainable = False\nmodel.get_layer(&#x27;shared&#x27;).trainable = False\nmodel.layers[3] = LoRALayer(model.get_layer(&#x27;lm_head&#x27;))</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0321","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-062-14-2-the-keras-loralayer","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s044","q":"Why does Demo 1's <code>layer = LoRALayer(layer)</code> loop not add LoRA to the model?","a":"<p>Inside the loop, <code>layer = LoRALayer(layer)</code> only rebinds a local variable. It does not insert the LoRA layer into the model, so the loop effectively just freezes layers.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0322","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-062-14-2-the-keras-loralayer","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s044","q":"In the Chapter 4 LoRA small-model Solution, how is LoRA applied instead of looping over the decoder's dense layers?","a":"<p>The small-model Solution skips the loop and applies the same three freezes plus <code>model.layers[3] = LoRALayer(model.get_layer('lm_head'))</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0323","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-062-14-2-the-keras-loralayer","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s044","q":"Why is the trainable count after \"LoRA\" the same as after the plain freeze, and how do you check LoRA is really trainable?","a":"<p>The reported count of 24,674,304 equals 768 × 32,128, the <code>lm_head</code> size, which is identical to the plain freeze. Always confirm with <code>model.summary()</code> that <code>w_a</code> / <code>w_b</code> appear among the trainable weights.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0324","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-062-14-2-the-keras-loralayer","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s044","q":"What numbers does the lecture report for LoRA FLAN-T5 versus full fine-tuning?","a":"<p>Trainable parameters drop from 247,577,856 (944 MB) to 24,674,304 (94 MB), with 222,903,552 frozen. GPU RAM is about 8 GB versus about 30 GB. Training for 3 epochs takes 7–10 min versus 20–30 min for full fine-tuning.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0325","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-063-14-3-compile-train-evaluate","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s045","q":"What learning rate does LoRA training use compared with full fine-tuning, and which optimizer class?","a":"<p>A larger learning rate of 1e-3, with the <code>tf_keras</code> Adam optimizer, because Keras 3 and the Hugging Face TF models differ.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0326","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-063-14-3-compile-train-evaluate","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s045","q":"How do you compile and train the LoRA FLAN-T5 model?","a":"<p>Compile with <code>tf_keras</code> Adam at <code>learning_rate=1e-3</code> and <code>SparseCategoricalCrossentropy(from_logits=True)</code>, then fit for 3 epochs with validation data.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>model.compile(optimizer=tf_keras.optimizers.Adam(learning_rate=1e-3),\n              loss=tf.keras.losses.SparseCategoricalCrossentropy(from_logits=True))\nmodel.fit(train_dataset, validation_data=test_dataset, epochs=3)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0327","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-063-14-3-compile-train-evaluate","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s045","q":"How do you evaluate the LoRA model and what final loss is good?","a":"<p>Call <code>model.evaluate(test_dataset)</code>. The lecture's rule of thumb is that a final loss below 3.0 is good.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>model.evaluate(test_dataset)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0328","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-064-14-4-experiments-rank-batch-size-demo-2","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s046","q":"What does the Demo 2 LoRA experiment loop over?","a":"<p>Ranks <code>[1, 4, 16]</code> and batch sizes <code>[8, 64, 128]</code>, for 2 epochs each. The notebook uses a deliberately large learning rate of 1e-2, and freezes layers 0–2 by index.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>ranks = [1, 4, 16]\nbatch_sizes = [8, 64, 128]\nepochs = 2</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0329","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-064-14-4-experiments-rank-batch-size-demo-2","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s046","q":"How does <code>count_params</code> count trainable and non-trainable weights in Keras?","a":"<p>It sums the product of each weight's shape over <code>trainable_weights</code> and <code>non_trainable_weights</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>trainable_params = np.sum([np.prod(v.get_shape().as_list()) for v in model.trainable_weights])\nnon_trainable_params = np.sum([np.prod(v.get_shape().as_list()) for v in model.non_trainable_weights])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0330","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-064-14-4-experiments-rank-batch-size-demo-2","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s046","q":"How does the Demo 2 loop freeze layers and wrap the head for each run?","a":"<p>It reloads the model, sets layers 0, 1 and 2 to non-trainable, and wraps <code>lm_head</code> in a <code>LoRALayer</code> at index 3.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>model.layers[0].trainable = False\nmodel.layers[1].trainable = False\nmodel.layers[2].trainable = False\nmodel.layers[3] = LoRALayer(model.get_layer(&#x27;lm_head&#x27;))</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0331","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-064-14-4-experiments-rank-batch-size-demo-2","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s046","q":"What is the bug in the Demo 2 rank × batch-size experiment?","a":"<p>The loop never passes <code>rank</code> to <code>LoRALayer</code>, so every run uses the default rank 4. The experiment as written varies batch size only.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0332","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-064-14-4-experiments-rank-batch-size-demo-2","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s046","q":"How does the Demo 2 loop store and print results for each configuration?","a":"<p>It stores <code>history.history</code> in <code>results</code> keyed by <code>(rank, batch_size)</code>, then loops over <code>results.items()</code> and prints them.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>results[(rank, batch_size)] = history.history\nfor (rank, batch_size), history in results.items():</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0333","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-065-14-4-experiments-rank-batch-size-demo-2","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s046","q":"What effect do higher rank and higher batch size have in the Demo 2 experiments?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Higher rank</td><td>More stable training and better loss reduction, more parameters</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Higher batch size</td><td>Fewer steps, faster wall-clock, more memory</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0334","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-065-14-4-experiments-rank-batch-size-demo-2","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s046","q":"What did low rank with a small batch and high rank with a large batch give in the experiments?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Low rank + small batch</td><td>~2,500 steps, ~325 s, unstable training</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>High rank + large batch</td><td>~157 steps, ~200 s, stable training</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0335","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-065-14-4-experiments-rank-batch-size-demo-2","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s046","q":"Which layers does the lecture suggest targeting with LoRA first?","a":"<p>Dense layers first, and attention for more capacity. The final layers (<code>lm_head</code>) are often the most impactful.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0336","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-065-14-4-experiments-rank-batch-size-demo-2","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s046","q":"How do batch sizes of 8–16 compare with 64–128 in LoRA training?","a":"<p>Batch 8–16 is low-memory but unstable. Batch 64–128 is stable but memory-hungry.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0337","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-065-14-4-experiments-rank-batch-size-demo-2","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s046","q":"How do you deploy LoRA adapters?","a":"<p>Save only the LoRA adapters, combine them with the base model at inference, and swap adapters per task.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0338","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-066-14-5-challenge-flan-t5-small-lora-chapte","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s047","q":"What is the setup of the <code>Chapter4_Solution</code> challenge?","a":"<p>The same pipeline with flan-t5-small (76M parameters; structure: embedding → encoder → decoder → LM head). It freezes <code>shared</code>, <code>encoder</code>, <code>decoder</code> and wraps <code>lm_head</code>, counts parameters with TF ops, and trains 3 epochs at learning rate 1e-3 (batch 64 in the lecture variant). Then it computes BLEU.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0339","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-066-14-5-challenge-flan-t5-small-lora-chapte","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s047","q":"How do you load flan-t5-small as a TF model?","a":"<p>Use <code>TFAutoModelForSeq2SeqLM.from_pretrained</code> with <code>'google/flan-t5-small'</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>model = TFAutoModelForSeq2SeqLM.from_pretrained(&#x27;google/flan-t5-small&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0340","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-066-14-5-challenge-flan-t5-small-lora-chapte","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s047","q":"How do you count trainable and non-trainable parameters with TF ops?","a":"<p>Sum the product of each variable's shape over <code>trainable_variables</code> and <code>non_trainable_variables</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>trainable_params = tf.reduce_sum([tf.reduce_prod(v.shape) for v in model.trainable_variables])\nnon_trainable_params = tf.reduce_sum([tf.reduce_prod(v.shape) for v in model.non_trainable_variables])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0341","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-066-14-5-challenge-flan-t5-small-lora-chapte","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s047","q":"What results did the FLAN-T5-small LoRA challenge give?","a":"<p>Total 76M parameters, trainable about 16M (about 21%, the <code>lm_head</code>: 512 × 32,128). Training took about 3 min (about 40 s per epoch after warm-up). BLEU was about 0.11 and validation loss about 11.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0342","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-066-14-5-challenge-flan-t5-small-lora-chapte","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s047","q":"What BLEU would be very good for the FLAN-T5-small LoRA challenge, and how do you improve it?","a":"<p>0.3–0.4 would be very good, and larger models score higher. Scale up by switching to flan-t5-base or large.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0343","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-066-14-5-challenge-flan-t5-small-lora-chapte","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s047","q":"Which metric should you use to evaluate a summarisation model instead of BLEU?","a":"<p>ROUGE.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0344","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-067-15-chapter-5-exercises","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s048","q":"What do the three Chapter 5 solution notebooks apply?","a":"<p>The same \"freeze + train head/LoRA\" recipe on new tasks.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0345","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-067-15-chapter-5-exercises","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s048","q":"Which three tasks do the Chapter 5 exercises cover, and which notebooks hold the solutions?","a":"<p>Summarisation with LoRA (<code>Chapter5_Solution3</code>), sentiment analysis with DistilBERT on SST-2 (<code>Chapter5_Solution1</code>), and question answering with FLAN-T5 on SQuAD v2 (<code>Chapter5_Solution2</code>).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0346","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-068-15-1-summarisation-with-lora-chapter5-so","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s049","q":"What is the setup of the <code>Chapter5_Solution3</code> summarisation exercise?","a":"<p>FLAN-T5-small on CNN/DailyMail (<code>article</code> → <code>highlights</code>), with 10,000 train and 500 test rows, max length 512 and batch 128.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0347","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-068-15-1-summarisation-with-lora-chapter5-so","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s049","q":"Which parts of the summarisation exercise are the same as the translation LoRA notebooks?","a":"<p>Model loading, <code>LoRALayer</code>, the freeze/wrap loop, compile (<code>tf_keras</code> Adam 1e-3), fit (3 epochs) and the BLEU function.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0348","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-068-15-1-summarisation-with-lora-chapter5-so","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s049","q":"How do you load the CNN/DailyMail dataset, and what is the comment slip in the notebook?","a":"<p>Use <code>load_dataset('abisee/cnn_dailymail', '3.0.0')</code>. The comment says WMT16, but the dataset is CNN/DailyMail.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>dataset = load_dataset(&#x27;abisee/cnn_dailymail&#x27;, &#x27;3.0.0&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0349","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-068-15-1-summarisation-with-lora-chapter5-so","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s049","q":"How does the summarisation preprocessing build inputs and targets?","a":"<p>Inputs are <code>Summarize:</code> followed by the article, and targets are the highlights.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>inputs = [f&#x27;Summarize: {example}&#x27; for example in examples[&#x27;article&#x27;]]\ntargets = [example for example in examples[&#x27;highlights&#x27;]]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0350","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-068-15-1-summarisation-with-lora-chapter5-so","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s049","q":"What max length does the summarisation exercise use, and why does it differ from translation?","a":"<p>It uses 512 for inputs and labels, instead of 128 for translation.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>model_inputs = tokenizer(inputs, max_length=512, truncation=True, padding=&#x27;max_length&#x27;, return_tensors=&#x27;tf&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0351","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-068-15-1-summarisation-with-lora-chapter5-so","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s049","q":"How do you save the summarisation model?","a":"<p>Call <code>save_pretrained</code> with a folder path.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>model.save_pretrained(&#x27;./summarisation_model&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0352","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-068-15-1-summarisation-with-lora-chapter5-so","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s049","q":"How do you load the ROUGE metric and install its dependency for the summariser evaluation?","a":"<p>Install <code>rouge_score</code>, then load the metric with <code>load_metric(\"rouge\", trust_remote_code=True)</code>. Caveat: <code>load_metric</code> is removed in newer <code>datasets</code>; use <code>evaluate</code> instead.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>!pip install rouge_score\nrouge = load_metric(&quot;rouge&quot;, trust_remote_code=True)\nnum_samples = 1000</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0353","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-068-15-1-summarisation-with-lora-chapter5-so","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s049","q":"How does the summariser evaluation produce summaries with beam search 5?","a":"<p>It tokenizes the articles with max length 512 and calls <code>modified_t5_model.generate</code> with the attention mask, <code>max_length=128</code> and <code>num_beams=5</code>. <code>modified_t5_model</code> is the LoRA-adapted model.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>summaries = modified_t5_model.generate(inputs[&#x27;input_ids&#x27;], \n                                      attention_mask=inputs[&#x27;attention_mask&#x27;], \n                                      max_length=128, num_beams=5)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0354","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-068-15-1-summarisation-with-lora-chapter5-so","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s049","q":"How do you compute ROUGE for the summariser on 1,000 validation samples?","a":"<p>Take the <code>highlights</code> as references and call <code>rouge.compute</code> with the model's summaries as predictions. The result gives ROUGE-1, ROUGE-2 and ROUGE-L.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>val_summaries = [ex[&#x27;highlights&#x27;] for ex in val_dataset.take(num_samples)]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0355","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-069-15-2-sentiment-analysis-transfer-learnin","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s050","q":"What is the setup of the <code>Chapter5_Solution1</code> sentiment exercise?","a":"<p>An encoder-only model with a sequence classification head with 2 labels. It freezes the DistilBERT body (<code>model.layers[0]</code>) so only the classifier trains. It uses <code>from_logits=True</code> plus accuracy, then evaluates and saves.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0356","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-069-15-2-sentiment-analysis-transfer-learnin","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s050","q":"How do you load the SST-2 dataset and the DistilBERT tokenizer?","a":"<p>Use <code>load_dataset(\"stanfordnlp/sst2\")</code> and <code>AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(\"distilbert-base-uncased\")</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>dataset = load_dataset(&quot;stanfordnlp/sst2&quot;)\ntokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(&quot;distilbert-base-uncased&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0357","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-069-15-2-sentiment-analysis-transfer-learnin","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s050","q":"How does the SST-2 notebook tokenize the sentences?","a":"<p>It tokenizes the <code>sentence</code> field with padding to max length, truncation and <code>max_length=128</code>, applied with <code>dataset.map(..., batched=True)</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>return tokenizer(examples[&quot;sentence&quot;], padding=&#x27;max_length&#x27;, truncation=True, max_length=128, return_tensors=&#x27;tf&#x27;)\ntokenized_datasets = dataset.map(tokenize_function, batched=True)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0358","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-069-15-2-sentiment-analysis-transfer-learnin","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s050","q":"How does the SST-2 notebook convert the train split to a TF dataset?","a":"<p>It uses <code>to_tf_dataset</code> with <code>input_ids</code> and <code>attention_mask</code> as columns, <code>label</code> as the label column, shuffling and batch size 64.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>train_dataset = tokenized_datasets[&quot;train&quot;].to_tf_dataset(\n    columns=[&quot;input_ids&quot;, &quot;attention_mask&quot;],\n    label_cols=&quot;label&quot;,\n    shuffle=True,\n    batch_size=64\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0359","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-069-15-2-sentiment-analysis-transfer-learnin","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s050","q":"How do you load DistilBERT for sentiment classification with 2 labels and freeze its body?","a":"<p>Use <code>TFAutoModelForSequenceClassification.from_pretrained</code> with <code>num_labels=2</code>, then set <code>model.layers[0].trainable = False</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>model = TFAutoModelForSequenceClassification.from_pretrained(&quot;distilbert-base-uncased&quot;, num_labels=2)\nmodel.layers[0].trainable = False</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0360","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-069-15-2-sentiment-analysis-transfer-learnin","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s050","q":"How do you compile the DistilBERT SST-2 model?","a":"<p>Use Adam with learning rate 5e-5, <code>SparseCategoricalCrossentropy(from_logits=True)</code> and <code>SparseCategoricalAccuracy</code> as the metric.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>model.compile(\n    optimizer=tf.keras.optimizers.Adam(learning_rate=5e-5),\n    loss=tf.keras.losses.SparseCategoricalCrossentropy(from_logits=True),\n    metrics=tf.metrics.SparseCategoricalAccuracy(),\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0361","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-069-15-2-sentiment-analysis-transfer-learnin","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s050","q":"How do you train, save and evaluate the SST-2 model?","a":"<p>Fit for 3 epochs with validation data, save with <code>save_pretrained</code>, and call <code>evaluate</code> to read loss and accuracy.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>model.save_pretrained(&quot;./distilbert-sst2&quot;)\nresults = model.evaluate(validation_dataset)\nprint(f&quot;Test accuracy: {results[1]}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0362","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-069-15-2-sentiment-analysis-transfer-learnin","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s050","q":"What is mislabelled in the SST-2 notebook's evaluation?","a":"<p>It evaluates on the validation split but labels the result \"test\".</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0363","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-070-15-3-question-answering-flan-t5-on-squad","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s051","q":"Which packages does the FLAN-T5 SQuAD v2 exercise install?","a":"<p>transformers, datasets, tensorflow, rouge-score and nltk.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>!pip install transformers datasets tensorflow rouge-score nltk</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0364","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-070-15-3-question-answering-flan-t5-on-squad","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s051","q":"How does the SQuAD v2 exercise frame question answering for FLAN-T5?","a":"<p>As text-to-text QA. The input is <code>context + \" question: \" + question</code> and the target is the first answer text, or an empty string for unanswerable SQuAD v2 questions.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>inputs = [context + &quot; question: &quot; + question for question, context in zip(examples[&quot;question&quot;], examples[&quot;context&quot;])]\ntargets = [answer[&#x27;text&#x27;][0] if len(answer[&#x27;text&#x27;]) &gt; 0 else &quot;&quot; for answer in examples[&quot;answers&quot;]]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0365","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-070-15-3-question-answering-flan-t5-on-squad","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s051","q":"What is the setup of the <code>Chapter5_Solution2</code> QA exercise?","a":"<p>25,000 train and 2,000 validation rows, max length 512, and <code>DataCollatorForSeq2Seq</code> as <code>collate_fn</code>. It freezes the first three layers, uses learning rate 5e-2 for 3 epochs, and evaluates with ROUGE.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0366","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-070-15-3-question-answering-flan-t5-on-squad","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s051","q":"How do you load the SQuAD v2 dataset and the seq2seq data collator?","a":"<p>Use <code>load_dataset(\"squad_v2\")</code> and <code>DataCollatorForSeq2Seq(tokenizer, model=None)</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>dataset = load_dataset(&quot;squad_v2&quot;)\ndata_collator = DataCollatorForSeq2Seq(tokenizer, model=None)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0367","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-070-15-3-question-answering-flan-t5-on-squad","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s051","q":"How does the QA preprocessing tokenize targets and fill <code>labels</code> and <code>decoder_input_ids</code>?","a":"<p>It tokenizes the targets under <code>tokenizer.as_target_tokenizer()</code> with max length 512, and uses the label <code>input_ids</code> for both <code>labels</code> and <code>decoder_input_ids</code>. Caveat: <code>tokenizer.as_target_tokenizer()</code> is deprecated in favour of <code>text_target=</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>with tokenizer.as_target_tokenizer():\n    labels = tokenizer(targets, max_length=512, truncation=True, padding=&#x27;max_length&#x27;)\nmodel_inputs[&quot;labels&quot;] = labels[&quot;input_ids&quot;]\nmodel_inputs[&quot;decoder_input_ids&quot;] = labels[&quot;input_ids&quot;]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0368","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-070-15-3-question-answering-flan-t5-on-squad","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s051","q":"How do you select 25,000 train and 2,000 validation rows for SQuAD v2?","a":"<p>Use <code>select(range(...))</code> and <code>map(preprocess_function, batched=True)</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>train_dataset = dataset[&quot;train&quot;].select(range(25000)).map(preprocess_function, batched=True)\nvalidation_dataset = dataset[&quot;validation&quot;].select(range(2000)).map(preprocess_function, batched=True)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0369","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-071-15-3-question-answering-flan-t5-on-squad","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s051","q":"How do you load FLAN-T5-base and freeze its first three layers in the SQuAD v2 exercise?","a":"<p>Load with <code>TFAutoModelForSeq2SeqLM</code> and set <code>trainable = False</code> on <code>model.layers[:3]</code>, which are the embedding, encoder and decoder.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>model = TFAutoModelForSeq2SeqLM.from_pretrained(&quot;google/flan-t5-base&quot;)\nfor layer in model.layers[:3]:\n    layer.trainable = False</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0370","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-071-15-3-question-answering-flan-t5-on-squad","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s051","q":"What learning rate does the SQuAD v2 exercise use, and how does it compare with LoRA?","a":"<p>5e-2, which is very high. LoRA uses 1e-3.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>optimizer=tf.keras.optimizers.Adam(learning_rate=5e-2),</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0371","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-071-15-3-question-answering-flan-t5-on-squad","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s051","q":"How do you train and save the SQuAD v2 model?","a":"<p>Fit for 3 epochs with validation data and save with <code>save_pretrained</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>model.fit(\n    train_dataset,\n    validation_data=validation_dataset,\n    epochs=3\n)\nmodel.save_pretrained(&quot;./flan-t5-squad-v2&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0372","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-071-15-3-question-answering-flan-t5-on-squad","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s051","q":"Why does the QA exercise evaluate with ROUGE only instead of BLEU?","a":"<p>QA answers are short spans, so precision and recall of words matter more than BLEU's n-gram order. The notebook's print label still says \"Translation\".</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0373","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-071-15-3-question-answering-flan-t5-on-squad","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s051","q":"What is the gotcha in <code>answer = answer(batch)</code> in the SQuAD v2 evaluation?","a":"<p>It shadows the function <code>answer</code> with its result, so the cell cannot be re-run without restarting.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0374","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-072-16-multi-model-chatbot-with-flask","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s052","q":"What does the <code>Chapter5_Demo-Chatbot_Flask_App_with_Sentiment_Summarization_QA</code> app do?","a":"<p>It is a Flask app that combines four models behind one API and routes each message.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0375","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-072-16-multi-model-chatbot-with-flask","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s052","q":"How does the Flask chatbot route a message to a model?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Message</th><th>Model used</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Contains \"summarize\"</td><td>FLAN-T5-large summarisation (<code>summarize_text</code>)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Contains \"?\"</td><td>FLAN-T5-large Q&amp;A (<code>answer_question</code>)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Anything else</td><td>Fallback decoder-only model (<code>gpt2-large</code> text-generation pipeline)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Every message</td><td>DistilBERT SST-2 sentiment; if negative, the decoder prompt is prefixed with \"The user is angry. Their message: ...\"</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0376","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-072-16-multi-model-chatbot-with-flask","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s052","q":"What are the design points and limits of the Flask chatbot's state?","a":"<p>Models load once at startup. <code>conversation_history</code> and <code>conversation_summaries</code> are module-level globals, so the app is single-user and not thread-safe (demo only). <code>/reset</code> summarises, stores the summary and clears history. <code>/greet</code> greets.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0377","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-072-16-multi-model-chatbot-with-flask","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s052","q":"What does <code>%%writefile chatbot.py</code> do in the Colab notebook?","a":"<p>It writes the cell to <code>chatbot.py</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0378","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-072-16-multi-model-chatbot-with-flask","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s052","q":"Which packages does the chatbot notebook install?","a":"<p><code>transformers</code>, <code>flask</code>, <code>requests</code> and <code>tensorflow</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>!pip install transformers flask requests tensorflow</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0379","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-072-16-multi-model-chatbot-with-flask","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s052","q":"How does the chatbot load its sentiment model and tokenizer?","a":"<p>It loads <code>distilbert/distilbert-base-uncased-finetuned-sst-2-english</code> with <code>TFAutoModelForSequenceClassification</code> and <code>AutoTokenizer</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>sentiment_model = TFAutoModelForSequenceClassification.from_pretrained(&quot;distilbert/distilbert-base-uncased-finetuned-sst-2-english&quot;)\nsentiment_tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(&quot;distilbert/distilbert-base-uncased-finetuned-sst-2-english&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0380","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-072-16-multi-model-chatbot-with-flask","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s052","q":"Which models does the chatbot load for summarisation, question answering and generic fallback?","a":"<p>FLAN-T5-large for both summarisation and question answering, and a <code>gpt2-large</code> text-generation pipeline as the generic decoder-only model.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>summarization_model = TFAutoModelForSeq2SeqLM.from_pretrained(&quot;google/flan-t5-large&quot;)\nqa_model = TFAutoModelForSeq2SeqLM.from_pretrained(&quot;google/flan-t5-large&quot;)\npipe = pipeline(&quot;text-generation&quot;, model=&quot;gpt2-large&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0381","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-072-16-multi-model-chatbot-with-flask","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s052","q":"How does the chatbot app start the Flask app and hold conversation state?","a":"<p>It creates <code>Flask(__name__)</code> and two module-level lists, <code>conversation_history</code> and <code>conversation_summaries</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>app = Flask(__name__)\nconversation_history = []\nconversation_summaries = []</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0382","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-073-16-multi-model-chatbot-with-flask","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s052","q":"How does <code>summarize_text</code> in the chatbot summarise a text?","a":"<p>It prefixes the text with <code>Summarize:</code>, tokenizes with max length 512, and generates with <code>max_length=150</code>, <code>num_beams=4</code> and early stopping.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>inputs = summarization_tokenizer(f&#x27;Summarize: {text}&#x27;, return_tensors=&quot;tf&quot;, max_length=512, truncation=True, padding=True)\nsummary_ids = summarization_model.generate(inputs[&#x27;input_ids&#x27;], max_length=150, num_beams=4, early_stopping=True)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0383","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-073-16-multi-model-chatbot-with-flask","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s052","q":"How does <code>summarize_conversation</code> differ from <code>summarize_text</code>?","a":"<p>It joins the conversation list into one string with <code>\" \".join(conversation)</code> and allows a longer summary with <code>max_length=500</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>conversation_text = &quot; &quot;.join(conversation)\nsummary_ids = summarization_model.generate(inputs[&#x27;input_ids&#x27;], max_length=500, num_beams=4, early_stopping=True)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0384","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-073-16-multi-model-chatbot-with-flask","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s052","q":"How does <code>answer_question</code> in the chatbot prompt the QA model?","a":"<p>It builds the prompt <code>question: {question} answer: </code> and calls <code>generate</code> on the input ids.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>inputs = qa_tokenizer(f&#x27;question: {question} answer: &#x27;, return_tensors=&quot;tf&quot;)\nanswer_ids = qa_model.generate(inputs[&#x27;input_ids&#x27;])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0385","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-073-16-multi-model-chatbot-with-flask","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s052","q":"How does <code>analyze_sentiment</code> in the chatbot decide positive or negative?","a":"<p>It applies softmax to the logits and calls the text positive if the score for class 1 is above 0.5, otherwise negative.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>sentiment_score = tf.nn.softmax(outputs.logits, axis=-1).numpy()\nsentiment = &quot;positive&quot; if sentiment_score[0][1] &gt; 0.5 else &quot;negative&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0386","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-073-16-multi-model-chatbot-with-flask","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s052","q":"How does <code>generate_response</code> use sentiment in the chatbot?","a":"<p>If the sentiment is negative, the prompt becomes \"The user is angry. Their message: {message}\". Otherwise the prompt is the message itself.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>if sentiment == &quot;negative&quot;:\n    prompt = f&quot;The user is angry. Their message: {message}&quot;\nelse:\n    prompt = message</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0387","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-074-16-multi-model-chatbot-with-flask","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s052","q":"What does the chatbot's <code>/reset</code> route do?","a":"<p>It is a POST route. It summarises the conversation history, appends the summary to <code>conversation_summaries</code>, clears the history and returns a JSON message with the summary.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@app.route(&#x27;/reset&#x27;, methods=[&#x27;POST&#x27;])\nsummary = summarize_conversation(conversation_history)\nconversation_summaries.append(summary)\nconversation_history = []\nreturn jsonify({&quot;message&quot;: &quot;Conversation has been reset.&quot;, &quot;summary&quot;: summary})</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0388","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-074-16-multi-model-chatbot-with-flask","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s052","q":"What does the chatbot's <code>/greet</code> route do?","a":"<p>It is a GET route that returns a JSON greeting message.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>@app.route(&#x27;/greet&#x27;, methods=[&#x27;GET&#x27;])\nreturn jsonify({&quot;message&quot;: &quot;Hello! How can I assist you today?&quot;})</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0389","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-074-16-multi-model-chatbot-with-flask","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s052","q":"How does the chatbot's <code>/chat</code> route pick the task from the message?","a":"<p>It lowercases the message and checks for \"summarize\", then checks for \"?\", and otherwise uses the default response.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>if &quot;summarize&quot; in user_message.lower():\nelif &quot;?&quot; in user_message:\n    response = answer_question(user_message)\nelse:\n    response = generate_response(user_message)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0390","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-074-16-multi-model-chatbot-with-flask","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s052","q":"What does the <code>/chat</code> route store in the conversation history?","a":"<p>It appends <code>User: {user_message}</code> and <code>Agent: {response}</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>conversation_history.append(f&#x27;User: {user_message}&#x27;)\nconversation_history.append(f&#x27;Agent: {response}&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0391","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-074-16-multi-model-chatbot-with-flask","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s052","q":"What host and port does the chatbot app run on, and what is the caution?","a":"<p>It runs on <code>host='0.0.0.0'</code> and <code>port=5000</code>. That exposes the app on all interfaces, which is fine inside a throwaway Colab VM. Bind to <code>127.0.0.1</code> (or put it behind auth) anywhere else.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>app.run(host=&#x27;0.0.0.0&#x27;, port=5000)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0392","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-074-16-multi-model-chatbot-with-flask","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s052","q":"How do the lecture-note variants of the chatbot app differ?","a":"<p>They use the same routes. <code>/chat</code> routes on <code>message.endswith('?')</code>, <code>/reset</code> guards against an empty history, and a <code>FineTunedChatbot</code> class in the intro lecture routes by a <code>task</code> field (<code>sentiment</code>/<code>summarize</code>/<code>qa</code>) in the JSON body instead of by keyword.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0393","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-074-16-multi-model-chatbot-with-flask","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s052","q":"How do you run the chatbot in the background in a notebook and check the listening port?","a":"<p>Run it with <code>nohup</code> in the background and list listening sockets with <code>lsof</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>!nohup python chatbot.py &amp;\n!sudo lsof -i -P -n | grep LISTEN</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0394","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-074-16-multi-model-chatbot-with-flask","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s052","q":"How do you call the Flask chatbot's <code>/greet</code> and <code>/chat</code> endpoints from a Colab notebook?","a":"<p>Use <code>requests</code>: <code>get</code> for <code>/greet</code> and <code>post</code> with a JSON <code>message</code> for <code>/chat</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from requests import post, get\nresponse = get(f&quot;http://{ip}:5000/greet&quot;).json()\nresponse = post(f&quot;http://{ip}:5000/chat&quot;, json= {&#x27;message&#x27;: &#x27;What is the capital of France?&#x27;}).json()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0395","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-074-16-multi-model-chatbot-with-flask","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s052","q":"How do you get the Colab VM address to call the Flask chatbot?","a":"<p>Use <code>gethostbyname(gethostname())</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from socket import gethostname, gethostbyname\nip = gethostbyname(gethostname()) # 172.28.0.12</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0396","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-074-16-multi-model-chatbot-with-flask","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s052","q":"How do you reset the conversation through the API?","a":"<p>Send a POST to <code>/reset</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>response = post(f&quot;http://{ip}:5000/reset&quot;).json()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0397","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-074-16-multi-model-chatbot-with-flask","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s052","q":"Which models does the chatbot course intend to use, and which does the demo use?","a":"<p>The course intends your own fine-tuned models from earlier chapters. The demo uses ready-made checkpoints: <code>distilbert-base-uncased-finetuned-sst-2-english</code>, FLAN-T5-large and GPT-2-large.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0398","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-075-17-1-what-the-course-covered","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s053","q":"What are the three transformer architectures and their uses?","a":"<p>Encoder-decoder (seq2seq: translation, summarisation), encoder-only (classification/understanding, BERT-style) and decoder-only (generation, GPT-style). Match the architecture to the task and weigh efficiency against capability.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0399","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-075-17-1-what-the-course-covered","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s053","q":"Which application areas did the Fine-Tuning for LLMs course cover?","a":"<p>Healthcare (medical text), finance (risk, documents) and customer service (support, sentiment).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0400","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-075-17-1-what-the-course-covered","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s053","q":"In the Fine-Tuning for LLMs course wrap-up, what is the stated LoRA benefit?","a":"<p>90%+ fewer trainable parameters, which makes fine-tuning feasible on modest hardware.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0401","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-076-17-2-advanced-topics-and-trends","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s054","q":"What does few-shot / zero-shot learning offer?","a":"<p>Good performance from minimal examples, better generalisation, and a lower data barrier.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0402","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-076-17-2-advanced-topics-and-trends","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s054","q":"What is federated learning and where is it used?","a":"<p>Data stays on local devices and only model updates are shared, which is privacy-preserving and decentralised. It is used for healthcare, on-device mobile learning and cross-organisation collaboration.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0403","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-076-17-2-advanced-topics-and-trends","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s054","q":"What is multimodal AI, and how does a multimodal model process its inputs?","a":"<p>Multimodal AI combines text + image (visual QA, captioning) or text + audio (speech-to-text with context). It encodes each modality, fuses the features and feeds one model.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>combined_features = fusion_layer([text_features, image_features, audio_features])\nreturn multimodal_model(combined_features)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0404","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-076-17-2-advanced-topics-and-trends","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s054","q":"What are pruning, quantisation and knowledge distillation, and what do they give?","a":"<p>Pruning removes unneeded parameters, quantisation lowers numeric precision, and knowledge distillation teaches a smaller model. They bring lower latency, lower cost and edge deployment.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0405","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-076-17-2-advanced-topics-and-trends","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s054","q":"Which next topics did the Fine-Tuning for LLMs course name?","a":"<p>Chatbot cloud deployment, model optimisation (distillation, quantisation, pruning), scalable production AI services, Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), Constitutional AI and Mixture of Experts.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"fine-tuning-llm-f0406","card":"q-fine-tuning-llm-076-17-2-advanced-topics-and-trends","sec":"fine-tuning-llm-s054","q":"How can you stay current with the LLM field (arXiv, conferences, Hugging Face)?","a":"<p>Follow arXiv, conference proceedings (NeurIPS, ICML, ACL, EMNLP), and Hugging Face, Kaggle and Colab.</p>","hand":true}];
